WEBVTT

﻿1
00:01:15.857 --> 00:01:19.905
I would say the biggest hurdle for me.

2
00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:24.779
is gettin' past the
embarrassment of it all.

3
00:01:28.174 --> 00:01:30.524
It's hard to talk about who I used to be.

4
00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:36.139
Not a day goes by

5
00:01:39.403 --> 00:01:40.273
that I'm not grateful.

6
00:01:40.447 --> 00:01:43.363
I mean. I mean to my bones

7
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:46.627
about how my life turned around.

8
00:01:53.547 --> 00:01:54.374
Shoot.

9
00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.987
We've been into some pretty
dark places together.

10
00:02:02.556 --> 00:02:03.383
I mean.

11
00:02:06.473 --> 00:02:07.779
you turned it around.

12
00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.174
made a life for yourself.

13
00:02:16.266 --> 00:02:18.398
I guess I just wanted to know

14
00:02:21.793 --> 00:02:23.229
how you did that?

15
00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:32.369
You hear these rare stories. you know?

16
00:02:32.543 --> 00:02:34.109
Of how the impossible happened.

17
00:02:37.504 --> 00:02:38.331
Well.

18
00:02:40.246 --> 00:02:42.553
this is one of those stories.

19
00:03:13.975 --> 00:03:16.891
Hey!

20
00:03:50.577 --> 00:03:54.320
It was the 1950s. but if
you pulled up to our yard.

21
00:03:54.494 --> 00:03:57.062
you would've thought it was the 1850s.

22
00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.456
That's how poor we were.

23
00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.241
Dad spent most of his time
workin' in the oil fields.

24
00:04:02.415 --> 00:04:04.112
I wish you didn't always have to go.

25
00:04:04.287 --> 00:04:06.637
Hell. that's life. Phil.

26
00:04:06.811 --> 00:04:08.073
It's time you grew up.

27
00:04:12.077 --> 00:04:13.644
Take care of things around here.

28
00:04:15.602 --> 00:04:16.211
You got it?

29
00:04:16.386 --> 00:04:17.256
Yes. sir.

30
00:04:24.611 --> 00:04:25.438
Who's a man?

31
00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.137
I'm a man.

32
00:04:29.312 --> 00:04:31.401
Mama provided a different
set of challenges.

33
00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.405
- When she had one of her spells.
- Mom. stop it!

34
00:04:35.579 --> 00:04:36.319
- Get outta here!
- You'll go back

35
00:04:36.493 --> 00:04:37.102
to the hospital again!

36
00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:38.669
Get out!

37
00:04:38.843 --> 00:04:39.887
All we could really
do is get outta the way.

38
00:04:40.061 --> 00:04:40.845
No one's takin' me to the hospital.

39
00:04:41.019 --> 00:04:42.194
You gotta calm down!

40
00:04:42.368 --> 00:04:43.804
Please!

41
00:04:43.978 --> 00:04:45.110
Get outta here!

42
00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.154
Go!

43
00:04:48.418 --> 00:04:51.246
I started at a
young age. a very young age.

44
00:04:53.379 --> 00:04:55.163
Come to the woods and bringin'
back somethin' you could eat.

45
00:04:57.122 --> 00:05:00.647
Squirrel. ducks. quail.
doves. whatever was there.

46
00:05:01.996 --> 00:05:03.258
The woods became my home.

47
00:05:05.043 --> 00:05:07.306
Sometimes I would just
sit there for hours.

48
00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:08.568
listen to the woods.

49
00:05:09.613 --> 00:05:13.225
They would talk and I
would try and talk back.

50
00:05:17.795 --> 00:05:19.100
I could get lost in them.

51
00:05:20.798 --> 00:05:22.321
They were my refuge.

52
00:05:25.411 --> 00:05:30.416
But sooner or later. the real
world always comes knockin'.

53
00:06:16.984 --> 00:06:18.595
No. no!

54
00:06:18.769 --> 00:06:20.335
No. no!
- Phil!

55
00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:21.685
They're takin' her away again!
- You can't make me!

56
00:06:21.859 --> 00:06:24.078
You can't make me. you can't!

57
00:06:24.252 --> 00:06:25.428
No!

58
00:06:25.602 --> 00:06:26.516
Phil!

59
00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:27.604
Phil. don't let 'em take me!

60
00:06:27.778 --> 00:06:29.214
She ain't done nothin' wrong!

61
00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:31.738
Judy. Judy!

62
00:06:31.912 --> 00:06:33.348
Phil. Phil. Phil!

63
00:06:35.481 --> 00:06:38.571
Mom!

64
00:06:38.745 --> 00:06:39.529
Phil!

65
00:06:39.703 --> 00:06:41.705
Phil. Phil!

66
00:07:01.942 --> 00:07:04.815
She was gone for months at a time.

67
00:07:04.989 --> 00:07:06.338
Mama?

68
00:07:06.512 --> 00:07:08.035
While they tried the
only medicine they had.

69
00:07:09.994 --> 00:07:11.169
shock treatment.

70
00:07:12.387 --> 00:07:13.388
Mama?

71
00:07:25.009 --> 00:07:25.966
Why does she keep doin' this stuff

72
00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:27.490
if she knows they'll lock her up?

73
00:07:28.882 --> 00:07:30.362
She can't help it.

74
00:07:30.536 --> 00:07:31.929
It's in her blood or somethin'.

75
00:07:33.104 --> 00:07:34.497
We got that blood in us?

76
00:07:36.542 --> 00:07:38.152
Don't know.

77
00:07:38.326 --> 00:07:40.067
but we'll always look out
for each other. won't we?

78
00:07:40.981 --> 00:07:42.287
You mean that. Phil?

79
00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:45.377
Of course I do. Jan.

80
00:07:47.161 --> 00:07:48.859
Si. go get some taters
from under the house.

81
00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:50.121
Nah. nah. nah.

82
00:07:50.295 --> 00:07:52.427
Hey. last time that possum ran after me.

83
00:07:52.602 --> 00:07:55.039
his teeth were like this big.

84
00:08:00.871 --> 00:08:01.915
I didn't know it at the time.

85
00:08:02.089 --> 00:08:04.657
but just up the road a few miles lived

86
00:08:04.831 --> 00:08:06.006
a girl who would soon become

87
00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:08.879
the most important person in my life.

88
00:08:11.359 --> 00:08:12.491
Kay Carroway.

89
00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:14.841
Oh. damn it!

90
00:08:15.015 --> 00:08:16.451
Language. Mom!

91
00:08:16.626 --> 00:08:17.888
Kay. pick up your toys.
they nearly killed me.

92
00:08:18.062 --> 00:08:19.716
and then you go get those over there.

93
00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.326
- Compared to us.
- Stay on your feet.

94
00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.849
- Kay was rich.
- gonna be stockin'

95
00:08:23.023 --> 00:08:23.633
the store tonight. and I
can't do it without you.

96
00:08:23.807 --> 00:08:24.895
Oh-

97
00:08:25.069 --> 00:08:26.070
They owned the general store in town.

98
00:08:26.244 --> 00:08:28.551
so we equated that with filthy rich.

99
00:08:28.725 --> 00:08:31.597
Y'all could close stores on
Sundays and come to church.

100
00:08:31.771 --> 00:08:33.643
It'd be good for your soul. Daddy.

101
00:08:33.817 --> 00:08:36.123
Sunday's our best day. Katie-bug.

102
00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.865
You may say a prayer for us.

103
00:08:39.039 --> 00:08:40.650
especially about sellin'
them three roasts today

104
00:08:40.824 --> 00:08:43.348
before I have to throw 'em
out and lose money on 'em.

105
00:08:44.218 --> 00:08:45.089
Hey?

106
00:08:46.351 --> 00:08:47.526
Don't you get caught readin'

107
00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.094
them pioneer books in church again.

108
00:08:52.052 --> 00:08:53.880
Just in case.

109
00:08:54.054 --> 00:08:55.490
"Little House on the
Prairie." new edition.

110
00:08:55.665 --> 00:08:57.188
I don't have this one.

111
00:08:57.362 --> 00:08:58.145
I know.

112
00:08:58.319 --> 00:08:59.277
Says there's all kinds

113
00:08:59.451 --> 00:09:00.887
of new maps and drawings in there.

114
00:09:01.061 --> 00:09:02.019
Thanks. Daddy.

115
00:09:05.718 --> 00:09:08.112
Kay wasn't like the other kids.

116
00:09:08.286 --> 00:09:09.461
They judged us.

117
00:09:10.331 --> 00:09:11.506
She didn't.

118
00:09:20.777 --> 00:09:23.214
I guess she saw somethin' else.

119
00:09:25.433 --> 00:09:28.349
Look like the riff-raff's
blowing in from the field.

120
00:09:28.523 --> 00:09:30.525
Y'all should be ashamed of yourselves.

121
00:09:31.526 --> 00:09:34.181
Wowie. look at this.

122
00:09:34.355 --> 00:09:35.618
What are these called?

123
00:09:35.792 --> 00:09:36.749
Hubcaps.

124
00:09:36.923 --> 00:09:38.403
Dang!

125
00:09:38.577 --> 00:09:40.318
Pa's truck ain't never had these.

126
00:09:41.885 --> 00:09:44.061
Must be a load of
millionaires here in town.

127
00:09:48.021 --> 00:09:49.109
Turns out there was somethin'

128
00:09:49.283 --> 00:09:51.198
besides huntin' I was actually good at.

129
00:09:52.373 --> 00:09:53.331
I was born with it.

130
00:09:54.985 --> 00:09:57.640
That's how I became the
high school quarterback.

131
00:10:04.734 --> 00:10:06.779
Down. set. hut!

132
00:10:23.709 --> 00:10:24.754
Hey. way to play fellas.

133
00:10:24.928 --> 00:10:25.885
You gotta stop runnin' like that.

134
00:10:26.059 --> 00:10:27.670
You put me out of a job.

135
00:10:27.844 --> 00:10:28.758
Pretty sure you gotta get on the field

136
00:10:28.932 --> 00:10:31.499
before you can lose that job. son.

137
00:10:31.674 --> 00:10:33.501
Talk about your pioneer man. Kay.

138
00:10:34.328 --> 00:10:36.026
Maybe he'll walk you off
the field after the game.

139
00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.636
Phil Robertson. the quarterback?

140
00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.290
You gotta be kiddin' me.

141
00:10:39.464 --> 00:10:41.074
I seen the way he looks at you.

142
00:10:41.248 --> 00:10:42.685
Hey. Phil
Robertson. can I get a statement?

143
00:10:43.773 --> 00:10:44.904
Nah. nah.

144
00:10:45.078 --> 00:10:46.514
You wanna talk to Si Robertson right here.

145
00:10:46.689 --> 00:10:47.864
Real hero of the game.

146
00:10:48.038 --> 00:10:48.952
Si Robertson?

147
00:10:49.126 --> 00:10:50.605
Did you even play?

148
00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:52.346
Boy. did I even play?

149
00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:54.087
I was so fast like lightning.

150
00:10:54.261 --> 00:10:55.349
that's why it probably didn't even feel

151
00:10:55.523 --> 00:10:57.047
like you saw me out there on that field.

152
00:10:57.221 --> 00:10:59.049
Miss Kay Carroway.

153
00:10:59.223 --> 00:11:00.137
Hey. Phil.

154
00:11:00.311 --> 00:11:01.225
Hey.

155
00:11:02.356 --> 00:11:03.967
Look. I know we don't know
each other all that well.

156
00:11:04.141 --> 00:11:07.492
but think maybe I could walk
you off the field tonight?

157
00:11:07.666 --> 00:11:08.362
I'd like that.

158
00:11:09.755 --> 00:11:10.756
Okay.

159
00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.366
So we walked off the field together

160
00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.064
and she offered me a ride home.

161
00:11:14.934 --> 00:11:16.501
I didn't even have the luxury of goin'

162
00:11:16.675 --> 00:11:18.764
on my first date without
at least one third wheel.

163
00:11:18.938 --> 00:11:20.331
And that's when I went down to pet

164
00:11:20.505 --> 00:11:22.855
what I thought was a
dog. and no way. okay?

165
00:11:23.029 --> 00:11:25.162
Turned out it was a five-pound squirrel.

166
00:11:25.336 --> 00:11:26.729
Sorry about this.

167
00:11:26.903 --> 00:11:28.861
I mean. I really do despise beavers.

168
00:11:29.035 --> 00:11:32.082
but I also respect their
work ethic and determination.

169
00:11:36.608 --> 00:11:37.914
You're gonna stay in the car.

170
00:11:38.088 --> 00:11:39.959
- What do you mean?
- This is my date.

171
00:11:40.133 --> 00:11:41.221
so you're stayin'.

172
00:11:41.395 --> 00:11:43.093
I'll be skin and bone if I don't eat.

173
00:11:43.267 --> 00:11:44.181
I hate to break it to ya.
honey. but you already are.

174
00:11:44.355 --> 00:11:46.270
Hey Jack. I am wastin' away.

175
00:11:46.444 --> 00:11:47.401
All right. fine. fine.

176
00:11:47.575 --> 00:11:48.925
Quit your yappin'.

177
00:11:49.099 --> 00:11:49.621
I'll get you somethin'.
but you're stayin' here.

178
00:11:49.795 --> 00:11:50.665
All right.

179
00:11:54.278 --> 00:11:55.105
All right.

180
00:11:58.238 --> 00:11:59.718
Sorry about that.

181
00:11:59.892 --> 00:12:01.589
♪ Yeah. yeah. yeah. yeah ♪

182
00:12:12.644 --> 00:12:13.993
I know girls are supposed to act

183
00:12:14.167 --> 00:12:15.081
like they don't eat
nothin' on these dates.

184
00:12:15.255 --> 00:12:17.692
but I am absolutely starvin'.

185
00:12:17.867 --> 00:12:18.563
Hey. Rachel?

186
00:12:18.737 --> 00:12:20.260
Hey. Kay.

187
00:12:20.434 --> 00:12:22.132
Could I get two muffy
sandwiches and a large fry?

188
00:12:22.306 --> 00:12:23.176
What you want? I can pay.

189
00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.134
Hey. no. come on.

190
00:12:24.308 --> 00:12:26.440
You drove. I got this.

191
00:12:29.704 --> 00:12:31.794
Uh. you know. I don't really
eat after the games anyway.

192
00:12:31.968 --> 00:12:34.448
so I think I'm just gonna
get something for Si. so.

193
00:12:35.798 --> 00:12:36.494
You know what?

194
00:12:36.668 --> 00:12:38.452
I changed my mind.

195
00:12:38.626 --> 00:12:40.019
Could you just gimme one of
those single grilled cheeses.

196
00:12:40.193 --> 00:12:42.239
and Rachel. you owe me
a fry from last week.

197
00:12:42.413 --> 00:12:43.718
so don't go cheatin' out on me again.

198
00:12:43.893 --> 00:12:45.503
Okay.

199
00:12:45.677 --> 00:12:47.418
Fries are for skinny bones.

200
00:12:51.117 --> 00:12:52.162
In those days.

201
00:12:52.336 --> 00:12:53.293
it was a nightmare dealin' with Mama.

202
00:12:53.467 --> 00:12:55.121
Where is it?

203
00:12:55.295 --> 00:12:57.863
When she was good. she was
great. Funny. sharp. kind.

204
00:12:58.037 --> 00:12:59.343
Ma. what are you lookin' for?

205
00:12:59.517 --> 00:13:00.823
The money.

206
00:13:00.997 --> 00:13:02.433
Where's the money?

207
00:13:02.607 --> 00:13:03.651
I keep tellin' you.
we ain't got no money.

208
00:13:03.826 --> 00:13:05.871
At least not in the way you're sayin'.

209
00:13:06.045 --> 00:13:07.090
Oh no. from your pa.

210
00:13:07.264 --> 00:13:08.482
He's been sendin' it.

211
00:13:08.656 --> 00:13:10.267
But when it wasn't her day-

212
00:13:10.441 --> 00:13:11.703
I got back
from the hospital and-

213
00:13:11.877 --> 00:13:13.748
Life was hell for all of us.

214
00:13:13.923 --> 00:13:15.620
Yes. Mama. and Pa did send it.

215
00:13:15.794 --> 00:13:16.839
We've been usin' it.

216
00:13:17.013 --> 00:13:18.188
Jan needed actual clothes for school.

217
00:13:18.362 --> 00:13:20.407
Si needed shoes for football.

218
00:13:20.581 --> 00:13:22.801
Everything around us costs money.

219
00:13:26.413 --> 00:13:27.327
Why are you wearing that?

220
00:13:27.501 --> 00:13:28.589
Why are you all dressed up?

221
00:13:30.983 --> 00:13:32.855
'Cause I got a date tonight.

222
00:13:34.334 --> 00:13:36.293
You got a date?

223
00:13:36.467 --> 00:13:38.817
Oh. baby. with who. huh?

224
00:13:41.559 --> 00:13:42.821
Kay Carroway.

225
00:13:46.651 --> 00:13:47.608
Carroway?

226
00:13:50.089 --> 00:13:52.178
That rich family in town?

227
00:13:55.007 --> 00:13:56.269
Well. that's nice.

228
00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:03.668
You gonna leave me. Phil?

229
00:14:03.842 --> 00:14:05.278
You gonna leave me. Phil?

230
00:14:05.452 --> 00:14:06.758
Is that what you're gonna do?

231
00:14:06.932 --> 00:14:07.585
- I'm not leave-
- You gonna leave me?

232
00:14:07.759 --> 00:14:09.239
I'm not leavin'!

233
00:14:13.243 --> 00:14:14.984
Don't go.

234
00:14:15.158 --> 00:14:16.159
Don't go.

235
00:14:16.333 --> 00:14:19.031
Don't go like your father.

236
00:14:26.821 --> 00:14:29.302
- Hey.
- Hey. you ready to go?

237
00:14:31.087 --> 00:14:31.914
What's wrong?

238
00:14:33.045 --> 00:14:33.741
Nothin'.

239
00:14:33.916 --> 00:14:35.526
Everything's fine.

240
00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:36.440
No. I can tell you look
like you've seen a ghost.

241
00:14:36.614 --> 00:14:37.484
What...

242
00:14:38.616 --> 00:14:40.705
Oh. my Mama's been
actin' up again is all.

243
00:14:40.879 --> 00:14:42.272
but it's fine. we got our date tonight.

244
00:14:42.446 --> 00:14:43.273
It's...

245
00:14:45.884 --> 00:14:47.016
There's just a lot goin' on.

246
00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:50.062
Hey. whoa. it's okay.

247
00:14:50.236 --> 00:14:51.759
We can figure it out together.

248
00:14:52.847 --> 00:14:53.674
No. no. all right?

249
00:14:53.848 --> 00:14:55.502
You shouldn't...

250
00:14:55.676 --> 00:14:56.982
No. you're not gonna have
to deal with any of this.

251
00:14:57.156 --> 00:14:58.505
Hey. who needs another
muffy at Fertitta's?

252
00:14:58.679 --> 00:14:59.854
I've got an idea.

253
00:15:03.249 --> 00:15:05.077
Thank you again for bringin' all this.

254
00:15:05.251 --> 00:15:06.992
Well. just because my
parents own a grocery store

255
00:15:07.166 --> 00:15:08.863
don't mean I know how
to cook anything in it.

256
00:15:09.038 --> 00:15:11.127
Well. honey. that I can teach.

257
00:15:11.301 --> 00:15:12.650
Always start with some butter here.

258
00:15:12.824 --> 00:15:14.391
baby. okay?

259
00:15:14.565 --> 00:15:15.958
Give us a snack. all right?

260
00:15:16.132 --> 00:15:17.350
No one-
- Coca-Cola?

261
00:15:17.524 --> 00:15:19.483
Dang. she is rich.
- Jan!

262
00:15:19.657 --> 00:15:20.527
Where's the tea?

263
00:15:22.616 --> 00:15:23.835
Hey. grab me somethin'. would ya?

264
00:15:24.009 --> 00:15:25.141
Hey. I hear that.

265
00:15:25.315 --> 00:15:26.969
You steal a bite before it's ready.

266
00:15:27.143 --> 00:15:28.448
I'm gonna swat you upside
the head with this spatula.

267
00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.975
Hand me those beans. will ya?

268
00:15:33.149 --> 00:15:35.847
Okay. so make sure this is lump free.

269
00:15:36.021 --> 00:15:37.501
- Smells good.
- Thank you.

270
00:15:37.675 --> 00:15:39.894
now get out.

271
00:15:40.069 --> 00:15:43.289
Okay. take one of these and make sure

272
00:15:43.463 --> 00:15:45.639
that's against the knives.

273
00:15:47.032 --> 00:15:48.599
Soaked up with flour.

274
00:15:49.513 --> 00:15:50.601
However you wanna do that.

275
00:15:50.775 --> 00:15:52.342
I do it kinda messy. but some people...

276
00:15:56.737 --> 00:15:59.044
Kay. thank you for tonight.

277
00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:02.178
It really meant a lot to my mama.

278
00:16:02.352 --> 00:16:05.703
and though she probably won't admit it.

279
00:16:07.357 --> 00:16:10.012
she really misses my pa
when he's on the job.

280
00:16:10.186 --> 00:16:11.665
Yeah. yeah.

281
00:16:11.839 --> 00:16:13.102
You know. she seemed okay.

282
00:16:14.538 --> 00:16:16.931
There's this other
side to her. you know?

283
00:16:17.106 --> 00:16:18.237
And you can't predict it.

284
00:16:18.411 --> 00:16:19.847
It just kinda-

285
00:16:20.022 --> 00:16:21.893
You ain't never have
to be ashamed of that.

286
00:16:24.461 --> 00:16:25.984
Wait. shh. shh.

287
00:16:26.158 --> 00:16:27.203
- What is it?
- Hear that?

288
00:16:28.943 --> 00:16:32.686
That's a pintail.

289
00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.087
You love it out here.

290
00:16:43.219 --> 00:16:44.046
I do.

291
00:16:45.743 --> 00:16:47.223
It is beautiful.

292
00:16:54.578 --> 00:16:56.710
We can get a place out here. you and I.

293
00:16:57.711 --> 00:16:58.712
a little shack up on the river

294
00:16:58.886 --> 00:17:00.671
and I could spend my days fishin'.

295
00:17:01.715 --> 00:17:03.108
I...

296
00:17:06.503 --> 00:17:07.286
I'm sorry.

297
00:17:08.766 --> 00:17:10.637
A girl like you definitely
don't wanna spend

298
00:17:10.811 --> 00:17:11.725
her time like that.

299
00:17:14.032 --> 00:17:16.861
My dad used to read me
pioneer stories every night.

300
00:17:17.035 --> 00:17:18.689
What's a pioneer story?

301
00:17:18.863 --> 00:17:21.039
You know. like movin' out
west. livin' off the land.

302
00:17:21.213 --> 00:17:23.302
makin' your own butter. that kinda thing.

303
00:17:24.216 --> 00:17:26.392
There's always a good love story too.

304
00:17:26.566 --> 00:17:27.959
I used to go to bed dreamin'

305
00:17:28.133 --> 00:17:30.179
about how amazin' that
kinda life would be.

306
00:17:30.353 --> 00:17:34.270
So. yeah. a little place by the
river would be just the thing.

307
00:17:36.794 --> 00:17:39.405
You really are the perfect
woman. Miss Kay Carroway.

308
00:17:43.627 --> 00:17:46.108
Kay fell right in with my family.

309
00:17:46.282 --> 00:17:48.762
In my mind. we were a perfect fit.

310
00:17:51.591 --> 00:17:53.985
Phil has been an All-State
quarterback this year.

311
00:17:54.159 --> 00:17:55.247
They've been saying he's gonna

312
00:17:55.421 --> 00:17:56.857
get lots of offers from colleges to play.

313
00:17:57.031 --> 00:18:00.600
Football is such a rough sport to me.

314
00:18:00.774 --> 00:18:02.428
Seems like a waste of time.

315
00:18:02.602 --> 00:18:05.649
I mean. are they gonna pay
you a lot of money to play?

316
00:18:05.823 --> 00:18:07.955
I'm sure they got scholarships and such.

317
00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:09.392
Am I right. Phil?

318
00:18:09.566 --> 00:18:10.741
Oh. yes. Sir.

319
00:18:10.915 --> 00:18:12.046
Yes. Ma'am.

320
00:18:12.221 --> 00:18:14.440
See. there you go. Wanita.

321
00:18:16.529 --> 00:18:18.749
You know. that reminds me.

322
00:18:18.923 --> 00:18:22.231
Kay. guess who came into the store today?

323
00:18:24.276 --> 00:18:26.017
Mrs. Watson.

324
00:18:26.191 --> 00:18:28.976
Now. her boy is nearly
outta medical school.

325
00:18:29.151 --> 00:18:31.065
A doctor. you know?

326
00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:34.721
And I remember. oo. he
used to come around.

327
00:18:34.895 --> 00:18:36.723
He had eyes for you.

328
00:18:39.509 --> 00:18:41.859
Wanita. you look like
you're runnin' empty there.

329
00:18:42.033 --> 00:18:44.601
Well. so is my beer.

330
00:18:45.645 --> 00:18:47.256
I would love another.

331
00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.518
Phil. wait!

332
00:18:48.692 --> 00:18:49.693
I'm sorry about my Mama.

333
00:18:49.867 --> 00:18:50.998
Phil!
- You ain't gotta

334
00:18:51.173 --> 00:18:52.522
be polite anymore. Kay.
- Please!

335
00:18:52.696 --> 00:18:54.611
Just. I'm sorry about my Mama. okay?

336
00:18:54.785 --> 00:18:56.308
This not gonna work.

337
00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.530
It's huntin' season.
- No.

338
00:19:00.704 --> 00:19:01.835
- I gotta go.
- No.

339
00:19:09.974 --> 00:19:12.716
So. you just broke up
with her just like that?

340
00:19:13.934 --> 00:19:15.153
It was huntin' season.

341
00:19:19.766 --> 00:19:21.203
- That's a bad move.
- Yep.

342
00:19:22.639 --> 00:19:23.988
One of many.

343
00:19:28.035 --> 00:19:29.341
How'd you get her back then?

344
00:19:29.515 --> 00:19:33.215
Hey!

345
00:19:33.389 --> 00:19:35.391
Now!

346
00:20:13.559 --> 00:20:14.734
Phil!

347
00:20:14.908 --> 00:20:16.170
Phil. it's Kay!

348
00:20:29.183 --> 00:20:31.142
The death of Kay's
father came out of nowhere

349
00:20:31.316 --> 00:20:33.579
and left a big hole in her family.

350
00:20:35.886 --> 00:20:36.756
Kay.

351
00:20:39.237 --> 00:20:40.107
I love you.

352
00:20:41.326 --> 00:20:43.154
I'm sorry for runnin' off like that.

353
00:20:46.592 --> 00:20:47.593
It wasn't long after her daddy died

354
00:20:47.767 --> 00:20:49.769
that her mama spiraled down quickly.

355
00:20:49.943 --> 00:20:52.119
She fought a hard battle with alcohol.

356
00:20:52.294 --> 00:20:54.078
and the alcohol eventually won.

357
00:20:54.992 --> 00:20:56.210
I was all she had.

358
00:20:56.385 --> 00:20:59.126
but in a lot of ways she was all I had.

359
00:20:59.997 --> 00:21:00.824
Wait.

360
00:21:02.086 --> 00:21:02.913
You think it's right that we're doin' this

361
00:21:03.087 --> 00:21:04.523
when we ain't married?

362
00:21:07.918 --> 00:21:12.879
I. Phil Robertson promise to
love and be with you forever.

363
00:21:15.186 --> 00:21:18.798
I. Kay Carroway promise to
love and be with you forever.

364
00:21:20.409 --> 00:21:22.280
♪ Just one kiss from your sweet lips ♪

365
00:21:22.454 --> 00:21:24.456
♪ Will tell me that your love real ♪

366
00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.023
So after all that.

367
00:21:26.197 --> 00:21:27.851
because of my skillset
throwin' a football.

368
00:21:28.025 --> 00:21:30.201
I headed off to Louisiana Tech.

369
00:21:31.594 --> 00:21:33.335
Great game. boys!

370
00:21:33.509 --> 00:21:35.293
Kay was only a junior
in high school at the time.

371
00:21:35.467 --> 00:21:37.339
but we had a baby on the way.

372
00:21:38.688 --> 00:21:40.254
and it was pretty rough on Kay.

373
00:21:42.909 --> 00:21:44.868
Tried to balance takin' care of my family

374
00:21:45.042 --> 00:21:49.786
and school and football.
but it was too much.

375
00:21:51.265 --> 00:21:53.224
Eventually I had to quit football.

376
00:21:53.398 --> 00:21:55.008
You ever think about that. man?

377
00:21:55.182 --> 00:21:56.619
You coulda been big.

378
00:21:56.793 --> 00:21:59.752
I'm talkin' like cereal box big.

379
00:21:59.926 --> 00:22:01.145
Wheaties big.

380
00:22:02.189 --> 00:22:04.583
"The" Terry Bradshaw was your number two.

381
00:22:04.757 --> 00:22:06.063
"The" Terry Bradshaw.

382
00:22:07.978 --> 00:22:10.633
I say it worked out pretty good for him.

383
00:22:10.807 --> 00:22:11.851
Yeah. I'd say so.

384
00:22:13.026 --> 00:22:14.332
Hey. you and him get along?

385
00:22:17.291 --> 00:22:19.685
Can I take
this thing off now. Phil?

386
00:22:19.859 --> 00:22:20.773
No.

387
00:22:20.947 --> 00:22:22.079
Can I at least sit up?

388
00:22:22.253 --> 00:22:23.689
I told ya if you wanna come out here.

389
00:22:23.863 --> 00:22:25.212
this is how it's gonna be.

390
00:22:27.214 --> 00:22:28.346
Yeah. I thought you were joking.

391
00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:30.435
I never joke about fishin'.

392
00:22:30.609 --> 00:22:32.742
Can't be givin' away my secret spots.

393
00:22:32.916 --> 00:22:33.917
not even to you.

394
00:22:36.789 --> 00:22:38.269
All right. take it off.

395
00:22:38.443 --> 00:22:39.836
- Yeah?
- Yeah. now.

396
00:22:40.010 --> 00:22:41.185
♪ Saturday night we're goin' fishin' ♪

397
00:22:41.359 --> 00:22:42.665
Woo!

398
00:22:42.839 --> 00:22:44.144
Got my hair all messed
up and everything. man.

399
00:22:44.318 --> 00:22:45.624
You're fine.

400
00:22:45.798 --> 00:22:47.713
Take a look.

401
00:22:47.887 --> 00:22:49.019
♪ Don't forget the frying pan
and bring along some manners ♪

402
00:22:49.193 --> 00:22:50.368
Sorta special.

403
00:22:50.542 --> 00:22:52.239
♪ And we'll cook 'em up for dinner ♪

404
00:22:52.414 --> 00:22:53.719
♪ Rollin' up and fryin' up ♪

405
00:22:53.893 --> 00:22:55.721
- Yeah. that's called a fish.
- Woo hoo!

406
00:22:55.895 --> 00:22:59.899
♪ We're gonna go fishin'
next Saturday night ♪

407
00:23:00.073 --> 00:23:01.901
I think my release is
gettin' a lot better.

408
00:23:02.075 --> 00:23:03.599
I've been hangin' around
after practice every day.

409
00:23:03.773 --> 00:23:04.687
workin' on it.

410
00:23:06.079 --> 00:23:07.820
You really love football.
don't you Bradshaw?

411
00:23:07.994 --> 00:23:09.256
Yeah. I do.

412
00:23:09.431 --> 00:23:11.041
More than anything.

413
00:23:11.215 --> 00:23:12.651
Just feels like it's part
of my blood or somethin'.

414
00:23:12.825 --> 00:23:15.088
I feel like that with huntin'.

415
00:23:15.262 --> 00:23:17.177
That's why I ain't playin'
next year.

416
00:23:17.351 --> 00:23:18.222
What?

417
00:23:18.396 --> 00:23:19.919
Are you serious?

418
00:23:20.093 --> 00:23:21.268
NFL scouts have been
watchin' you all year long.

419
00:23:21.443 --> 00:23:22.531
Everybody knows you'll go pro.

420
00:23:22.705 --> 00:23:23.532
Nah.

421
00:23:24.489 --> 00:23:25.359
I'm done.

422
00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:27.100
It's your turn.

423
00:23:28.928 --> 00:23:30.452
You think I'm ready?

424
00:23:30.626 --> 00:23:32.062
Of course you're ready.

425
00:23:32.236 --> 00:23:33.933
No one can throw a bomb
down the field like you.

426
00:23:34.107 --> 00:23:36.022
You're the Blonde Bomber.

427
00:23:37.023 --> 00:23:38.416
The Blonde Bomber?

428
00:23:41.114 --> 00:23:43.987
Guess that's better than
the name you gave Johnson.

429
00:23:44.161 --> 00:23:45.554
What. you mean Old Stubby?

430
00:23:45.728 --> 00:23:47.381
Why you gotta
do him like that. Phil?

431
00:23:47.556 --> 00:23:49.383
It ain't my fault he got
them stubby little legs.

432
00:23:49.558 --> 00:23:51.734
- Shoot.
- So. I lost my scholarship.

433
00:23:51.908 --> 00:23:54.954
but still managed to finish college.

434
00:23:55.128 --> 00:23:58.480
It was easy enough to
find a job in those days.

435
00:23:58.654 --> 00:24:00.569
The hard part was findin'
one that paid enough.

436
00:24:02.092 --> 00:24:04.355
Our family was growin'.

437
00:24:04.529 --> 00:24:05.617
Hey. boys!

438
00:24:05.791 --> 00:24:06.705
And so were the bills.

439
00:24:06.879 --> 00:24:07.837
Aw. I missed you boys.

440
00:24:08.011 --> 00:24:09.795
Come here. come here.

441
00:24:14.365 --> 00:24:15.235
How you been. huh?

442
00:24:15.409 --> 00:24:17.411
Boy. you gettin' heavy.

443
00:24:17.586 --> 00:24:18.804
Those feet smell?

444
00:24:18.978 --> 00:24:20.545
Boy. they smell bad!

445
00:24:20.719 --> 00:24:21.851
You need to take a shower.

446
00:24:23.374 --> 00:24:25.071
I'm gonna say hi to Mama. okay?

447
00:24:32.339 --> 00:24:36.213
- Hey. baby.
- Hey.

448
00:24:37.475 --> 00:24:38.694
How was your day. hm?

449
00:24:38.868 --> 00:24:41.827
It was good. until Alan tried to stick

450
00:24:42.001 --> 00:24:43.176
a crayon up Jase's nose.

451
00:24:45.222 --> 00:24:46.005
Did it fit?

452
00:24:46.179 --> 00:24:47.572
Hey! Phil!

453
00:24:59.802 --> 00:25:00.629
How's it lookin'?

454
00:25:04.197 --> 00:25:05.851
I can feed you out in the woods.

455
00:25:07.331 --> 00:25:09.028
I just need to make
sure we got enough money

456
00:25:09.202 --> 00:25:10.769
to keep a roof over our heads.

457
00:25:16.296 --> 00:25:21.258
I just don't wanna be gone
all the time like my dad was.

458
00:25:21.650 --> 00:25:22.520
You won't.

459
00:25:28.047 --> 00:25:31.007
You got two degrees from Louisiana Tech.

460
00:25:32.878 --> 00:25:34.184
You can do just about anything

461
00:25:34.358 --> 00:25:37.448
you set your mind to. Phil Robertson.

462
00:25:42.845 --> 00:25:43.672
Hey.

463
00:25:45.848 --> 00:25:47.284
I'm proud of you.

464
00:25:48.938 --> 00:25:49.852
I love you.

465
00:25:51.375 --> 00:25:52.768
And I love you.

466
00:25:59.905 --> 00:26:03.735
I wouldn't change anything about us.

467
00:26:03.909 --> 00:26:05.432
We gonna make it.

468
00:26:07.826 --> 00:26:09.828
Stick with me. Miss Kay.

469
00:26:10.002 --> 00:26:13.049
I'll put that long green in your pockets.

470
00:26:17.923 --> 00:26:19.055
Kay was definitely nervous

471
00:26:19.229 --> 00:26:21.623
about me havin' a job interview in a bar.

472
00:26:21.797 --> 00:26:22.754
Was that me?

473
00:26:22.928 --> 00:26:24.321
Was- the bar interview was me?

474
00:26:24.495 --> 00:26:25.365
Yeah.

475
00:26:28.107 --> 00:26:29.152
it was you.

476
00:26:29.326 --> 00:26:30.719
Ah. I had a feelin'.

477
00:26:36.899 --> 00:26:38.770
Yeah. sorry about that.

478
00:26:42.556 --> 00:26:43.601
Good to see ya. Frank.

479
00:26:43.775 --> 00:26:46.648
Oh. oh. oh.

480
00:26:46.822 --> 00:26:48.301
Keep your hands to yourself. Big Al.

481
00:26:48.475 --> 00:26:49.433
You know I can't.

482
00:26:50.739 --> 00:26:53.089
Oh. hey. Sally. why don't you go ahead

483
00:26:53.263 --> 00:26:55.134
and grab me a shot of whiskey?

484
00:26:55.308 --> 00:26:57.659
Hey. you know. make it two.

485
00:26:57.833 --> 00:26:58.703
One for my friend Phil here.

486
00:26:58.877 --> 00:27:00.487
Hey. make it quick.

487
00:27:00.662 --> 00:27:04.578
- You got it.
- He's just catchin' up.

488
00:27:04.753 --> 00:27:06.450
Thank you. Mr. Bolen.

489
00:27:06.624 --> 00:27:07.494
Mr. Bolen?

490
00:27:08.887 --> 00:27:10.541
You must be lookin' for my daddy.

491
00:27:11.498 --> 00:27:12.630
You can call me Big Al.

492
00:27:13.718 --> 00:27:16.590
Okay. sure. Big Al.

493
00:27:17.679 --> 00:27:18.636
Ah.

494
00:27:18.810 --> 00:27:22.684
So. Phil. tell me about yourself.

495
00:27:22.858 --> 00:27:25.208
I got a wife and three
kids I need to support

496
00:27:25.382 --> 00:27:28.080
and teachin' always seemed
like a respectable thing to do.

497
00:27:28.254 --> 00:27:30.300
No. no. no. no.

498
00:27:30.474 --> 00:27:32.389
I don't mean that shit.

499
00:27:34.391 --> 00:27:35.871
I mean. tell me about you.

500
00:27:36.045 --> 00:27:38.656
What kinda man is Phil Robertson?

501
00:27:40.005 --> 00:27:42.704
Well. I love to hunt.

502
00:27:43.661 --> 00:27:45.402
Now. that's what I'm talkin' 'bout.

503
00:27:45.576 --> 00:27:48.753
Huntin's sure good up
around Junction City.

504
00:27:48.927 --> 00:27:51.147
Keep you real busy on the weekends.

505
00:27:51.321 --> 00:27:53.105
Somethin' to relieve the
stress of the teacher man.

506
00:27:53.279 --> 00:27:54.150
Hm.

507
00:27:58.545 --> 00:27:59.590
Need a smoke?

508
00:27:59.764 --> 00:28:01.592
Oh. I don't really smoke.

509
00:28:05.683 --> 00:28:08.686
Man. you got a sense
of humor. Phil Robertson.

510
00:28:21.046 --> 00:28:22.613
Hell. I knew we were
gonna get along just fine

511
00:28:22.787 --> 00:28:24.484
the moment I shook your hand.

512
00:28:29.620 --> 00:28:30.490
Thank you. Sally.

513
00:28:31.361 --> 00:28:33.493
Hey. and you best keep these comin'.

514
00:28:34.973 --> 00:28:35.844
We got a lot to celebrate tonight.

515
00:28:36.018 --> 00:28:36.845
All right.

516
00:28:38.629 --> 00:28:39.499
That's it?

517
00:28:40.326 --> 00:28:41.458
Did I get the job?

518
00:29:03.741 --> 00:29:06.744
My name is Mr. Robertson.

519
00:29:11.227 --> 00:29:14.230
If y'all could turn your
handbooks to page 45...

520
00:29:22.020 --> 00:29:23.761
Hey. there's my guy.

521
00:29:23.935 --> 00:29:26.329
How 'bout a drink.
celebrate the first day?

522
00:29:27.156 --> 00:29:28.722
I can't.

523
00:29:28.897 --> 00:29:30.942
Miss Kay's got a special
dinner waitin' for me tonight.

524
00:29:31.116 --> 00:29:31.856
Yeah. of course she does.

525
00:29:32.030 --> 00:29:33.292
She's a classy gal.

526
00:29:33.466 --> 00:29:34.598
Well. you ain't a dang derelict.

527
00:29:34.772 --> 00:29:36.643
I'm just talkin' about one drink.

528
00:29:36.818 --> 00:29:38.080
Hey. Fred.

529
00:29:38.254 --> 00:29:39.821
You didn't hear nothin'. Fred.

530
00:29:43.215 --> 00:29:45.522
One drink?

531
00:29:45.696 --> 00:29:46.653
One drink.

532
00:29:47.741 --> 00:29:49.047
Come on. then.

533
00:30:30.436 --> 00:30:31.307
Woo!

534
00:30:32.482 --> 00:30:33.570
- Yes!
- Woo!

535
00:30:47.323 --> 00:30:48.890
- All right.
- Woo!

536
00:30:49.064 --> 00:30:50.021
Line 'em up!

537
00:32:10.101 --> 00:32:13.975
This is as fresh as it
comes. Appaloosa catfish.

538
00:32:14.149 --> 00:32:16.020
That's the filet mignon of the river.

539
00:32:17.282 --> 00:32:19.458
- Jan!
- Hi. Kay.

540
00:32:19.632 --> 00:32:21.330
It's good to see you. sweetheart.

541
00:32:21.504 --> 00:32:22.548
- Hey. Phil.
- Hey. Jan.

542
00:32:22.722 --> 00:32:24.115
How you doin'?

543
00:32:24.289 --> 00:32:24.942
- I'm good. how are you?
- It's good to see you.

544
00:32:25.116 --> 00:32:26.291
You too.

545
00:32:26.465 --> 00:32:27.205
- Hey. hey. how you doin'?
- Hey.

546
00:32:27.379 --> 00:32:28.337
I'm Al.

547
00:32:28.511 --> 00:32:31.122
You must be one of Kay's friends.

548
00:32:31.296 --> 00:32:33.646
I know Phil ain't got
no good lookin' friends.

549
00:32:33.820 --> 00:32:35.344
Well. except for me. of course.

550
00:32:37.085 --> 00:32:37.737
That's my sister.

551
00:32:39.696 --> 00:32:41.350
Okay. okay.

552
00:32:41.524 --> 00:32:42.612
Oh. yeah. okay.

553
00:32:42.786 --> 00:32:43.787
All right.

554
00:32:43.961 --> 00:32:45.832
I mean. I was just bein' friendly.

555
00:32:46.007 --> 00:32:46.920
Why don't you be friendly

556
00:32:47.095 --> 00:32:49.227
in that direction over there. Al?

557
00:32:50.359 --> 00:32:51.186
Okay.

558
00:32:52.448 --> 00:32:54.145
- Sorry about him.
- No. I'm good.

559
00:32:54.319 --> 00:32:56.234
Hey. congratulations on your new job.

560
00:32:56.408 --> 00:32:57.409
I'm so proud of you.

561
00:32:57.583 --> 00:32:58.889
Thanks. Jan.

562
00:32:59.063 --> 00:33:00.717
Did Kay tell you we took the boys

563
00:33:00.891 --> 00:33:02.153
to church last weekend?

564
00:33:02.327 --> 00:33:03.285
They seemed to really enjoy it.

565
00:33:03.459 --> 00:33:05.069
You should come with us next time.

566
00:33:06.157 --> 00:33:08.464
Yeah. well. I like to spend

567
00:33:08.638 --> 00:33:11.162
my Sunday celebratin' God in other ways.

568
00:33:12.163 --> 00:33:16.167
Who needs a pew when you
can be out in His creation?

569
00:33:16.341 --> 00:33:18.996
Hey. y'all. how 'bout a toast. huh?

570
00:33:20.302 --> 00:33:22.130
To my man Phil Robertson here.

571
00:33:22.304 --> 00:33:26.786
the newest remedial English
teacher at Junction City High.

572
00:33:27.570 --> 00:33:29.093
He ain't smart but he pretty.

573
00:33:31.704 --> 00:33:33.445
I can't do. I can't deal.

574
00:33:33.619 --> 00:33:35.404
- Four ducks?
- Yeah. four ducks.

575
00:33:35.578 --> 00:33:36.622
Four ducks.

576
00:33:36.796 --> 00:33:37.841
One bullet can't take down four ducks.

577
00:33:38.015 --> 00:33:39.277
Oh. it can if you're Phil Robertson.

578
00:33:39.451 --> 00:33:41.149
Who's this new friend with him?

579
00:33:41.323 --> 00:33:42.802
That's Al.

580
00:33:44.935 --> 00:33:46.676
He's from his work.

581
00:33:46.850 --> 00:33:48.634
He runs their school.
- Oh. okay.

582
00:33:49.940 --> 00:33:50.897
Yeah. it's that easy.

583
00:33:51.768 --> 00:33:53.074
- Woo ee!
- Woo!

584
00:33:55.989 --> 00:33:56.729
Ow!

585
00:34:03.127 --> 00:34:04.911
Woo!
- Told you boys.

586
00:34:05.086 --> 00:34:07.914
One thing I'm better at
than fishin' is shootin'.

587
00:34:08.785 --> 00:34:09.829
You okay?

588
00:34:10.003 --> 00:34:11.092
- Yeah.
- This here

589
00:34:11.266 --> 00:34:14.399
is some genuine Three Creeks moonshine.

590
00:34:16.358 --> 00:34:17.228
All right.

591
00:34:28.848 --> 00:34:29.719
Daddy?

592
00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:33.288
You goin' huntin'?

593
00:34:34.245 --> 00:34:35.203
You bet ya.

594
00:34:36.987 --> 00:34:37.857
Can I come?

595
00:34:40.164 --> 00:34:41.513
You don't know the woods.

596
00:34:42.471 --> 00:34:44.299
You don't know huntin'.

597
00:34:44.473 --> 00:34:46.779
You could teach me.

598
00:34:54.483 --> 00:34:55.788
Go back to bed.

599
00:35:01.707 --> 00:35:04.667
The next few years were a
bit of a blur. I must admit.

600
00:35:06.886 --> 00:35:09.237
♪ Rumor spreadin' 'round ♪

601
00:35:09.411 --> 00:35:11.891
♪ In that Texas town ♪

602
00:35:12.065 --> 00:35:13.850
You said you know the guy
that owns this property?

603
00:35:14.024 --> 00:35:15.765
Yeah. I met him once.

604
00:35:15.939 --> 00:35:17.158
Well. I met his sister.

605
00:35:17.332 --> 00:35:19.943
♪ And you know what I'm talkin' about ♪

606
00:35:20.117 --> 00:35:21.684
♪ Just let me know ♪
if you wanna go ♪

607
00:35:21.858 --> 00:35:23.903
It was that feeling again.

608
00:35:24.077 --> 00:35:26.210
being pulled in multiple directions.

609
00:35:28.169 --> 00:35:30.519
Huntin'. partying. family.

610
00:35:30.693 --> 00:35:33.739
The drinkin' began to
overtake everything else.

611
00:35:33.913 --> 00:35:37.787
"Airplanes follow duck."

612
00:35:37.961 --> 00:35:39.832
♪ Well. I hear it's fine ♪

613
00:35:41.312 --> 00:35:43.009
I thought it was freedom to my worries.

614
00:35:43.967 --> 00:35:45.882
but it didn't free me from 'em.

615
00:35:46.056 --> 00:35:48.406
It just made me forget about them.

616
00:35:48.580 --> 00:35:49.581
♪ A hmm. hmm ♪

617
00:35:49.755 --> 00:35:52.715
♪ And I hear it's tight ♪

618
00:35:52.889 --> 00:35:54.064
♪ Most every night ♪

619
00:35:56.632 --> 00:35:57.981
♪ But now I might be mistaken ♪

620
00:36:07.077 --> 00:36:09.775
She just will not leave me alone.

621
00:36:11.560 --> 00:36:14.258
I've heard of worse problems than that.

622
00:36:14.432 --> 00:36:15.390
And all I could think was.

623
00:36:15.564 --> 00:36:17.435
"Man. I gotta lay off the sauce."

624
00:36:18.871 --> 00:36:19.872
They respected Phil Robertson.

625
00:36:20.046 --> 00:36:22.571
They know Phil Robertson was a man.

626
00:36:22.745 --> 00:36:23.833
Who's a man?

627
00:36:29.012 --> 00:36:31.144
You're so beautiful. Marleen.

628
00:36:37.368 --> 00:36:39.675
♪ Oh. no ♪

629
00:36:44.332 --> 00:36:47.160
You wasn't
callin' them ducks in. Phil.

630
00:36:47.335 --> 00:36:50.163
You was commandin' them to come in.

631
00:36:50.990 --> 00:36:52.557
Back again?

632
00:36:52.731 --> 00:36:53.906
You don't even have the
decency to hang around here?

633
00:36:54.080 --> 00:36:54.994
I'm cookin' you dinner.

634
00:36:55.168 --> 00:36:56.387
I'm cleanin' up after the kids-

635
00:36:56.561 --> 00:36:58.737
Keep your mouth shut!

636
00:36:58.911 --> 00:37:00.739
What. you can't even have
a conversation with me?

637
00:37:07.355 --> 00:37:08.312
Y'all don't need this.

638
00:37:10.532 --> 00:37:12.360
Class dismissed.

639
00:37:20.977 --> 00:37:22.718
Who's a man?

640
00:37:27.723 --> 00:37:30.291
I was hell-bent
on doin' things my own way.

641
00:37:31.335 --> 00:37:32.293
I always had been.

642
00:37:36.079 --> 00:37:37.428
So. when I had to figure out other ways

643
00:37:37.602 --> 00:37:39.300
to provide for the family.

644
00:37:39.474 --> 00:37:42.215
I went back to the places
that have always provided.

645
00:37:42.390 --> 00:37:44.479
the woods. and the river.

646
00:38:04.803 --> 00:38:06.544
- Take care.
- Oh.

647
00:38:08.503 --> 00:38:10.679
Miss Abaleen.

648
00:38:12.333 --> 00:38:14.378
Phil Robertson.

649
00:38:14.552 --> 00:38:15.640
You been stayin' outta trouble?

650
00:38:15.814 --> 00:38:16.989
Yes. Ma'am.

651
00:38:17.163 --> 00:38:18.077
How's your mama?

652
00:38:21.342 --> 00:38:22.081
She doin' just great.

653
00:38:22.255 --> 00:38:23.909
Kay and the kids?

654
00:38:24.083 --> 00:38:24.997
It's all good.

655
00:38:25.171 --> 00:38:26.042
Hey?

656
00:38:27.173 --> 00:38:28.784
Got a fresh catch for ya.

657
00:38:28.958 --> 00:38:30.438
You back on the water?

658
00:38:30.612 --> 00:38:31.787
I thought I heard you teachin' down

659
00:38:31.961 --> 00:38:33.571
at that school in Junction City?

660
00:38:33.745 --> 00:38:35.399
Yeah. yeah.

661
00:38:38.315 --> 00:38:40.448
Sabbatical. you know?

662
00:38:41.623 --> 00:38:43.102
Just a short break.

663
00:38:44.626 --> 00:38:46.236
I got myself plenty for the shop today.

664
00:38:46.410 --> 00:38:49.065
You know I don't like
throwin' out no unsold fish.

665
00:38:50.022 --> 00:38:51.763
This here's as fresh as it comes.

666
00:38:51.937 --> 00:38:54.418
You could put this on
special right up front.

667
00:38:57.900 --> 00:38:59.467
Caught no more than an hour ago.

668
00:39:03.558 --> 00:39:04.776
Have a look.

669
00:39:05.821 --> 00:39:06.996
Mm hm.

670
00:39:20.270 --> 00:39:21.053
I appreciate you-

671
00:39:21.227 --> 00:39:22.838
Mm hm.

672
00:39:23.012 --> 00:39:25.231
You best make sure Miss
Kay and the boys get this.

673
00:39:25.406 --> 00:39:26.363
Yes. Ma'am.

674
00:39:26.537 --> 00:39:27.451
Absolutely.

675
00:39:36.591 --> 00:39:37.418
Do.

676
00:39:39.202 --> 00:39:41.378
I'm ashamed to say most of that money

677
00:39:41.552 --> 00:39:44.120
I was makin' didn't go
to Kay and the kids.

678
00:39:44.294 --> 00:39:46.252
but we always found a way to make more.

679
00:39:50.256 --> 00:39:54.086
Hey. if nothin' else. we were creative.

680
00:39:55.479 --> 00:39:58.264
All right. y'all. all bets are in.

681
00:39:58.439 --> 00:40:01.224
Got a rivalry as old as time.

682
00:40:02.573 --> 00:40:05.271
Man versus machine!

683
00:40:05.446 --> 00:40:07.143
Steel versus muscle!

684
00:40:08.797 --> 00:40:11.495
Rubber versus some bare feet.

685
00:40:11.669 --> 00:40:14.411
- Mm hm!
- Yeah. Phil!

686
00:40:14.585 --> 00:40:17.153
- All right.
- Let's go. come on!

687
00:40:17.327 --> 00:40:18.502
Let's get
this show on the boat!

688
00:40:20.635 --> 00:40:21.810
Come on. Phil!

689
00:40:23.725 --> 00:40:27.032
- On your mark.
- You got this. buddy!

690
00:40:29.687 --> 00:40:30.688
get set.

691
00:40:34.213 --> 00:40:35.345
go!

692
00:40:42.700 --> 00:40:44.093
What you doin' there?

693
00:40:44.267 --> 00:40:45.094
Woo!

694
00:40:48.314 --> 00:40:50.229
Just like old times. gentlemen.

695
00:40:51.187 --> 00:40:53.929
Don't give me that sour look
like I'm tryin' to cheat ya.

696
00:40:54.103 --> 00:40:56.235
It's Hank's car and he bet against me.

697
00:40:56.409 --> 00:40:58.237
You think he hamstrung his own bet?

698
00:40:59.151 --> 00:41:01.589
Hey. come on. now. pay up.

699
00:41:01.763 --> 00:41:03.068
Fair and square.

700
00:41:03.982 --> 00:41:06.942
Hey. don't be bitter.

701
00:41:07.116 --> 00:41:08.421
You and I both know Hank's car

702
00:41:08.596 --> 00:41:10.032
ain't got the gun to come even close

703
00:41:10.206 --> 00:41:12.643
to outrunnin' you if you
only give him 20 yards.

704
00:41:13.818 --> 00:41:17.256
You give him 25. he's got you smoked.

705
00:41:19.171 --> 00:41:23.785
Well. that's their fault
for not askin' for 25.

706
00:41:27.223 --> 00:41:28.180
Man. ever since I known you.

707
00:41:28.354 --> 00:41:29.442
you ain't never changed.

708
00:41:29.617 --> 00:41:31.009
Hey. Phil?

709
00:41:31.183 --> 00:41:32.533
Double or nothin'.

710
00:41:34.273 --> 00:41:35.927
Hold my beer.

711
00:41:45.154 --> 00:41:46.503
Hey. Babe.

712
00:41:49.158 --> 00:41:51.595
Guess you decided to finally come home.

713
00:41:52.727 --> 00:41:54.511
I know it's late. I was...

714
00:41:55.599 --> 00:41:57.296
I was. uh.

715
00:41:58.646 --> 00:42:00.430
workin'.

716
00:42:01.518 --> 00:42:03.346
Sell some fish?

717
00:42:03.520 --> 00:42:04.739
Yep.

718
00:42:13.399 --> 00:42:14.966
What is this?

719
00:42:16.098 --> 00:42:18.361
That's money I made.

720
00:42:18.535 --> 00:42:20.885
Well. how much fish you sell?

721
00:42:21.059 --> 00:42:22.104
What do you mean?

722
00:42:23.105 --> 00:42:25.107
There's $11 here.

723
00:42:27.588 --> 00:42:31.809
I know. I musta spent
some of it. all right?

724
00:42:34.551 --> 00:42:37.946
Phil. we have three hungry boys.

725
00:42:38.816 --> 00:42:41.602
You put all this pressure on
me to stretch a few dollars.

726
00:42:43.429 --> 00:42:45.954
It is embarrassing havin' a line

727
00:42:46.128 --> 00:42:48.086
of people behind me in
the grocery store waitin'

728
00:42:48.260 --> 00:42:51.133
for me to put stuff back
because I can't afford it.

729
00:42:51.307 --> 00:42:53.222
It's fine.

730
00:42:53.396 --> 00:42:54.919
We're fine.

731
00:42:55.093 --> 00:42:56.747
The kids are fine.

732
00:43:00.142 --> 00:43:02.231
I don't think we are. Phil.

733
00:43:06.931 --> 00:43:10.500
Hm. I told you boys. I'm blessed.

734
00:43:10.674 --> 00:43:12.371
I cannot lose.

735
00:43:12.545 --> 00:43:14.417
Jesus don't be playin' no dice.

736
00:43:14.591 --> 00:43:15.679
Only person who can play dice

737
00:43:15.853 --> 00:43:17.638
like that is the devil .

738
00:43:18.639 --> 00:43:22.468
which will explain why you
riskin' your neck in this bar.

739
00:43:22.643 --> 00:43:23.731
Hm.

740
00:43:24.557 --> 00:43:26.734
Nah. it's 'cause I like the
music and the company better.

741
00:43:26.908 --> 00:43:29.171
- Mm.
- If you went next door.

742
00:43:29.345 --> 00:43:31.260
you'd think they closed the
bar and opened up a morgue.

743
00:43:31.434 --> 00:43:33.958
Really?

744
00:43:34.132 --> 00:43:36.613
Well. I heard that the
owners are lookin' to sell.

745
00:43:37.745 --> 00:43:38.615
Really?

746
00:43:39.921 --> 00:43:42.837
Well. it just so happens
I'm in need of a job.

747
00:43:43.011 --> 00:43:45.796
I said they were sellin'.

748
00:43:45.970 --> 00:43:47.406
not hirin'.

749
00:43:49.887 --> 00:43:50.714
They here now?

750
00:44:00.071 --> 00:44:01.290
Jim Perkins?

751
00:44:01.464 --> 00:44:02.334
Yeah.

752
00:44:03.901 --> 00:44:04.946
Phil Robertson.

753
00:44:05.120 --> 00:44:06.774
Nice to meet you.

754
00:44:06.948 --> 00:44:07.862
I heard y'all might be interested

755
00:44:08.036 --> 00:44:09.385
in doin' a little business.

756
00:44:10.778 --> 00:44:12.257
What. you wanna buy the bar?

757
00:44:13.128 --> 00:44:14.346
Well. thought we could talk about

758
00:44:14.520 --> 00:44:16.609
a bit more of a creative strategy.

759
00:44:19.569 --> 00:44:20.439
Hold on.

760
00:44:21.484 --> 00:44:22.790
Hold on.
- Phil!

761
00:44:27.142 --> 00:44:28.056
Keep 'em closed.

762
00:44:30.232 --> 00:44:31.363
Come on.

763
00:44:31.537 --> 00:44:32.800
- Can I open them?
- Not yet.

764
00:44:34.323 --> 00:44:37.500
Just a little further. little further.

765
00:44:40.633 --> 00:44:41.939
Keep 'em closed.

766
00:44:45.116 --> 00:44:46.161
Stand here.

767
00:44:46.335 --> 00:44:48.163
Don't open 'em till I tell ya.

768
00:44:48.337 --> 00:44:49.730
Why does it smell like urine?

769
00:44:55.039 --> 00:44:56.040
Hold on.

770
00:44:58.869 --> 00:44:59.522
Phil?

771
00:45:01.698 --> 00:45:03.352
Okay. open 'em.

772
00:45:09.532 --> 00:45:12.927
It's a bar.

773
00:45:13.101 --> 00:45:16.017
♪ I don't need ♪

774
00:45:16.191 --> 00:45:17.061
You bought a bar?

775
00:45:17.235 --> 00:45:18.628
♪ silver and gold ♪

776
00:45:18.802 --> 00:45:19.760
Sort of.

777
00:45:19.934 --> 00:45:22.937
Phil. we can't afford a bar.

778
00:45:23.111 --> 00:45:24.895
♪ I don't need ♪

779
00:45:25.069 --> 00:45:27.637
I can't even afford groceries.

780
00:45:27.811 --> 00:45:29.073
Don't worry about that.

781
00:45:30.205 --> 00:45:31.032
Look at this.

782
00:45:34.122 --> 00:45:37.125
This is a new start for us as a family.

783
00:45:37.299 --> 00:45:38.256
You been complainin' about money.

784
00:45:38.430 --> 00:45:40.693
we'll make some more money here.

785
00:45:40.868 --> 00:45:43.740
You been complainin' about
not spendin' time together.

786
00:45:43.914 --> 00:45:46.525
well. we'll all be here as a family.

787
00:45:49.137 --> 00:45:50.051
I don't know. Phil.

788
00:45:50.225 --> 00:45:51.052
Hey.

789
00:45:52.270 --> 00:45:53.445
I'll make it up to you.

790
00:45:55.926 --> 00:45:58.711
Kay. I'm gonna make it up to you.

791
00:46:00.626 --> 00:46:03.673
I know things didn't work
out with the teachin' job.

792
00:46:03.847 --> 00:46:05.327
and I was tired.

793
00:46:05.501 --> 00:46:07.851
I wasn't treatin' this family well.

794
00:46:10.680 --> 00:46:14.553
But this is a fresh start for
the Robertson family. okay?

795
00:46:15.772 --> 00:46:17.469
Alan and Jase. they can even help.

796
00:46:23.388 --> 00:46:26.652
Look. I know you're a good man.

797
00:46:26.827 --> 00:46:28.089
I fell in love with that.

798
00:46:32.310 --> 00:46:34.138
But it's the drinkin'.

799
00:46:35.923 --> 00:46:38.360
How's bein' in a bar gonna help with that?

800
00:46:39.578 --> 00:46:42.843
'Cause I'll be workin'. not drinkin'.

801
00:46:43.756 --> 00:46:47.760
Look. you'll keep an eye
on it. I'll keep on it.

802
00:46:50.502 --> 00:46:52.678
I'm gon' make this
work. I want it to work.

803
00:46:56.508 --> 00:46:59.860
You know you're the only one for me.

804
00:47:00.034 --> 00:47:02.688
♪ Darlin' all I need is you ♪

805
00:47:11.567 --> 00:47:12.524
I love you.

806
00:47:18.356 --> 00:47:23.361
I love you.

807
00:47:23.535 --> 00:47:26.147
First thing we gotta do

808
00:47:26.321 --> 00:47:27.757
is get that pee smell outta here though.

809
00:47:27.931 --> 00:47:29.628
'cause that is horrible.

810
00:47:32.196 --> 00:47:33.328
I agree.

811
00:47:33.502 --> 00:47:35.286
I thought I had it figured out.

812
00:47:36.548 --> 00:47:38.246
Finally I had arrived.

813
00:47:38.420 --> 00:47:39.987
A way to spend time with my family.

814
00:47:40.161 --> 00:47:42.554
makin' more money. and still get to hang

815
00:47:42.728 --> 00:47:45.340
with my buddies and run
with them all night long.

816
00:47:45.514 --> 00:47:48.256
Daddy. when have I dried enough glasses?

817
00:47:48.430 --> 00:47:49.605
That's the point.

818
00:47:49.779 --> 00:47:51.607
They drink 'em. we clean 'em.

819
00:47:51.781 --> 00:47:55.002
and the whole cycle starts all
over again till closin' time.

820
00:47:55.176 --> 00:47:56.481
You're doin' great. keep goin'.

821
00:47:56.655 --> 00:47:59.310
Hey. get some more peanuts in here.

822
00:48:00.268 --> 00:48:01.182
Okay.

823
00:48:01.356 --> 00:48:02.923
Hey. Phil. get over here.

824
00:48:03.097 --> 00:48:05.577
I got a couple of friends I would like

825
00:48:05.751 --> 00:48:07.405
to introduce you to.

826
00:48:10.669 --> 00:48:14.543
Miss Kay. I'm dyin' here.

827
00:48:14.717 --> 00:48:16.066
Hold on. Billy.

828
00:48:16.240 --> 00:48:17.633
Don't think I don't see you there actin'

829
00:48:17.807 --> 00:48:18.939
like you haven't already
drank the Mississippi

830
00:48:19.113 --> 00:48:20.897
and spent your paycheck tonight.

831
00:48:27.208 --> 00:48:29.297
Why don't you
scoot on over a little bit.

832
00:48:30.994 --> 00:48:32.213
I'm tired of your disrespect!

833
00:48:32.387 --> 00:48:33.866
What is disrespectful about askin' you

834
00:48:34.041 --> 00:48:35.912
to spend one day with your family?

835
00:48:36.086 --> 00:48:37.131
That's all you do!

836
00:48:37.305 --> 00:48:39.960
Nag. nag. nag. nag. nag!

837
00:48:40.134 --> 00:48:41.787
The boys wanna see their daddy!

838
00:48:41.962 --> 00:48:44.225
Oh. don't use your boys to guilt me!

839
00:48:46.705 --> 00:48:49.404
Don't act like I don't
know what you've been up to.

840
00:48:49.578 --> 00:48:51.536
You been out drinkin'
that moonshine again.

841
00:48:51.710 --> 00:48:52.842
I can see it in your eyes.

842
00:48:53.016 --> 00:48:54.713
What the hell does that matter to you?

843
00:48:54.887 --> 00:48:57.107
'Cause it makes you
act like a wild animal.

844
00:48:57.281 --> 00:48:58.456
Oh. you wanna see a wild animal?

845
00:48:58.630 --> 00:48:59.762
Here you go!

846
00:49:29.052 --> 00:49:33.187
Uncle Si!

847
00:49:36.755 --> 00:49:37.582
Come here. boys!

848
00:49:37.756 --> 00:49:40.542
What about it?

849
00:49:40.716 --> 00:49:41.847
Oh. man.

850
00:49:42.718 --> 00:49:44.502
Oh. look at you.

851
00:49:44.676 --> 00:49:46.678
Man. y'all growin' faster than
green grass through a goose.

852
00:49:46.852 --> 00:49:48.028
We missed you. Uncle Si.

853
00:49:48.202 --> 00:49:49.464
Oh. buddy. I missed you. too.

854
00:49:49.638 --> 00:49:51.161
I missed you. too.

855
00:49:51.335 --> 00:49:52.293
Where's your mama?

856
00:49:52.467 --> 00:49:53.772
- Inside.
- Miss Kay!

857
00:49:58.081 --> 00:49:59.169
You can't catch me. Jase.

858
00:50:01.171 --> 00:50:03.913
- Get him. Alan!
- Tag. you're it.

859
00:50:07.090 --> 00:50:09.832
- Tag.
- Oh. I got you back.

860
00:50:10.006 --> 00:50:11.355
He becomes the devil. Si.

861
00:50:12.530 --> 00:50:14.532
Mm hm.

862
00:50:14.706 --> 00:50:16.273
I've seen it in his eyes.

863
00:50:19.276 --> 00:50:20.625
But it ain't him.

864
00:50:22.236 --> 00:50:24.934
You know that ain't your brother.

865
00:50:27.067 --> 00:50:29.895
Yeah. well. maybe not.
but I mean. come on.

866
00:50:30.070 --> 00:50:31.332
you don't deserve this.

867
00:50:33.073 --> 00:50:34.944
You're raisin' three boys on your own.

868
00:50:38.774 --> 00:50:41.255
I don't know what I deserve.

869
00:50:44.649 --> 00:50:48.218
Besides. what would
leavin' do to the boys?

870
00:50:49.654 --> 00:50:50.829
They love their daddy.

871
00:50:51.003 --> 00:50:52.527
Go long. Jase!

872
00:50:52.701 --> 00:50:53.571
Okay.

873
00:50:55.617 --> 00:50:58.054
I know it sounds crazy. Si.

874
00:51:00.317 --> 00:51:02.841
but I just know deep in my heart

875
00:51:06.193 --> 00:51:07.716
this family is gon' work out.

876
00:51:19.249 --> 00:51:20.120
Well.

877
00:51:22.165 --> 00:51:23.210
you know he ain't gonna change.

878
00:51:23.384 --> 00:51:24.863
not unless he stops drinkin'.

879
00:51:26.996 --> 00:51:27.866
I know.

880
00:51:32.697 --> 00:51:37.311
But you know. my Nanny
told me that someday

881
00:51:38.573 --> 00:51:40.792
you gonna have to fight for your marriage.

882
00:51:44.187 --> 00:51:47.277
When things get tough. that's what you do.

883
00:51:51.455 --> 00:51:52.195
You fight.

884
00:52:02.553 --> 00:52:05.730
Excuse me. ladies. gimme one second.

885
00:52:09.778 --> 00:52:10.605
Hey. Phil?

886
00:52:14.435 --> 00:52:15.871
There's someone here to see you.

887
00:52:26.273 --> 00:52:27.665
Who's responsible for this?

888
00:52:27.839 --> 00:52:30.146
Do you know where you'd
go if you die tonight?

889
00:52:31.147 --> 00:52:31.843
Jan?

890
00:52:33.193 --> 00:52:34.759
Hi. Phil.

891
00:52:34.933 --> 00:52:36.718
What you doin' here. Jan?

892
00:52:36.892 --> 00:52:39.024
Well. you ain't returned
my calls in forever.

893
00:52:39.199 --> 00:52:40.809
so I thought I'd check in on you.

894
00:52:42.158 --> 00:52:43.725
This your new boyfriend?

895
00:52:43.899 --> 00:52:47.468
Phil Robertson. this
is Pastor Bill Smith.

896
00:52:48.425 --> 00:52:51.167
How you doin' there. Phil?

897
00:52:51.341 --> 00:52:53.822
What ya sellin' preacher man?

898
00:52:53.996 --> 00:52:58.392
Naw. we ain't sellin'
nothin'. just offerin'.

899
00:52:59.436 --> 00:53:01.438
Just God and the good news.

900
00:53:03.962 --> 00:53:05.790
Don't you read "Times Magazine?"

901
00:53:06.922 --> 00:53:07.966
God is dead.

902
00:53:10.578 --> 00:53:12.493
Yeah. that's not been my experience.

903
00:53:13.798 --> 00:53:17.367
But I have been in here less than maybe

904
00:53:17.541 --> 00:53:20.979
a minute or two and I can already see

905
00:53:21.153 --> 00:53:23.460
you got one mighty chip on your shoulder.

906
00:53:30.119 --> 00:53:31.903
I should knock you out right here.

907
00:53:32.948 --> 00:53:34.210
You can try.

908
00:53:34.384 --> 00:53:35.255
Oh.

909
00:53:37.169 --> 00:53:38.388
Tall words from a preacher man

910
00:53:38.562 --> 00:53:41.086
who can't do nothin' about it.

911
00:53:42.349 --> 00:53:44.089
Jesus says I got to forgive you.

912
00:53:46.831 --> 00:53:50.400
but that don't mean he
won't forgive me. too.

913
00:53:50.574 --> 00:53:51.401
Phil.

914
00:53:53.229 --> 00:53:56.363
Jan. why you bringin' a
preacher man around here?

915
00:53:58.278 --> 00:54:01.455
Well. I heard you might be needin' one.

916
00:54:04.196 --> 00:54:06.024
Preachers ain't welcome 'round here.

917
00:54:07.983 --> 00:54:08.940
Let's go. Jan.

918
00:54:10.725 --> 00:54:12.204
He ain't ready yet.

919
00:54:12.379 --> 00:54:13.510
How you doin'. Ma'am?

920
00:54:13.684 --> 00:54:14.642
Excuse me.
- Jan. you should stay.

921
00:54:14.816 --> 00:54:16.208
Have a drink.

922
00:54:16.383 --> 00:54:17.949
I'm gonna be prayin' for you.

923
00:54:20.822 --> 00:54:22.606
Then you'll be wastin' your time.

924
00:54:24.173 --> 00:54:26.218
All right then.

925
00:54:26.393 --> 00:54:28.090
All right. God bless yourself.

926
00:54:35.880 --> 00:54:36.968
You put her up to it.

927
00:54:37.142 --> 00:54:38.622
I didn't.

928
00:54:38.796 --> 00:54:40.320
I swear. I didn't know
she was comin' around.

929
00:54:40.494 --> 00:54:41.973
Don't lie to me.

930
00:54:42.147 --> 00:54:43.975
I saw the way she was lookin' at you.

931
00:54:46.717 --> 00:54:48.850
This is just you tryin' to control me.

932
00:54:49.024 --> 00:54:49.764
All of you.

933
00:54:49.938 --> 00:54:52.332
Phil. please. please.

934
00:54:52.506 --> 00:54:54.943
I swear to God. you better
hold that tongue of yours.

935
00:54:55.117 --> 00:54:56.814
Phil. you're hurtin' my arm.

936
00:54:56.988 --> 00:54:58.816
If I found out you been tellin'
people about our business-

937
00:54:58.990 --> 00:55:00.775
Phil. you're hurtin' me.

938
00:55:18.445 --> 00:55:19.837
What'll it be. boys?

939
00:55:20.011 --> 00:55:21.404
Hm?

940
00:55:21.578 --> 00:55:23.711
Hey. sweetheart. that
pie recipe she gave me.

941
00:55:23.885 --> 00:55:25.669
my boys. they go crazy for it.

942
00:55:25.843 --> 00:55:26.844
They do.

943
00:55:28.150 --> 00:55:29.107
Where you been?

944
00:55:29.281 --> 00:55:31.066
Pretty late for grocery shoppin'.

945
00:55:31.240 --> 00:55:33.198
Well. when am I supposed to go?

946
00:55:33.373 --> 00:55:35.026
Been at the bar all day. Phil.

947
00:55:35.200 --> 00:55:36.854
You were with him. weren't ya?

948
00:55:37.028 --> 00:55:38.943
What are you talkin' about?

949
00:55:39.117 --> 00:55:39.857
That guy from the bar.

950
00:55:43.295 --> 00:55:44.558
Phil. I'm tired.

951
00:55:44.732 --> 00:55:46.908
It's been a long day and you been drinkin'

952
00:55:47.082 --> 00:55:48.910
through most of it.

953
00:55:49.084 --> 00:55:51.913
My drinkin' ain't got
nothin' to do with it.

954
00:55:52.087 --> 00:55:54.524
How long you been
runnin' 'round on me. hm?

955
00:55:54.698 --> 00:55:56.874
Answer the damn question.

956
00:55:58.093 --> 00:56:00.443
I ain't runnin' around on you.

957
00:56:01.401 --> 00:56:02.837
I know you're lyin'.

958
00:56:04.621 --> 00:56:06.754
Phil. I ain't havin'
this conversation now.

959
00:56:06.928 --> 00:56:08.146
Not when you're drunk.

960
00:56:08.320 --> 00:56:09.409
I ain't the problem.

961
00:56:10.366 --> 00:56:11.585
You're the problem.

962
00:56:11.759 --> 00:56:13.369
You're ruinin' my life!

963
00:56:13.543 --> 00:56:14.979
Oh. yeah?

964
00:56:15.153 --> 00:56:18.330
Well. you been ruinin' mine for 10 years!

965
00:56:21.638 --> 00:56:22.465
Get out.

966
00:56:24.772 --> 00:56:26.556
Get out and take your kids with you.

967
00:57:02.897 --> 00:57:04.028
Good Lord. Phil.

968
00:57:06.291 --> 00:57:07.728
I can't hardly believe that.

969
00:57:12.907 --> 00:57:16.127
I can't believe the thought
of what I did most days.

970
00:57:20.828 --> 00:57:23.047
But that was a point
where I'd lost it all.

971
00:57:25.746 --> 00:57:26.573
Kay.

972
00:57:29.140 --> 00:57:29.967
the boys.

973
00:57:31.621 --> 00:57:32.492
the bar.

974
00:57:34.319 --> 00:57:35.190
Bingo.

975
00:57:36.844 --> 00:57:38.106
Just like that.

976
00:58:07.831 --> 00:58:09.746
Kay. what's happenin'?

977
00:58:09.920 --> 00:58:11.095
What's goin' on? Come in.

978
00:58:11.269 --> 00:58:12.444
Come on in.

979
00:58:28.852 --> 00:58:29.679
Thanks.

980
00:58:34.902 --> 00:58:36.643
You can stay as long as you want.

981
00:58:40.168 --> 00:58:42.039
I can't trouble you like that.

982
00:58:42.213 --> 00:58:44.912
Trust me. it's no trouble at all.

983
00:58:46.957 --> 00:58:49.090
You're not worried
about Phil findin' out?

984
00:58:51.353 --> 00:58:52.441
He kicked you out.

985
00:58:58.229 --> 00:59:00.710
Why don't you go freshen up?

986
00:59:00.884 --> 00:59:02.059
I'll listen for Willie.

987
00:59:10.285 --> 00:59:11.155
Thank you. Jan.

988
00:59:12.243 --> 00:59:13.244
Of course.

989
01:01:09.621 --> 01:01:11.406
Are you okay. Mama?

990
01:01:14.583 --> 01:01:15.976
Mama?

991
01:01:16.150 --> 01:01:16.977
Hey.

992
01:01:18.326 --> 01:01:19.631
What's goin' on?

993
01:01:19.806 --> 01:01:21.242
It's Mama.

994
01:01:24.985 --> 01:01:27.683
Okay. okay. just go
back to bed. all right?

995
01:01:27.857 --> 01:01:28.510
Back to bed.

996
01:01:28.684 --> 01:01:29.554
I'll check.

997
01:01:34.255 --> 01:01:35.517
Kay?

998
01:01:41.653 --> 01:01:45.353
Kay. are you all right?

999
01:02:22.782 --> 01:02:26.524
I was thinkin' about
somethin' real stupid.

1000
01:02:34.837 --> 01:02:36.621
I was about to do it.

1001
01:02:39.755 --> 01:02:44.760
I just kept thinkin' about
those boys.

1002
01:02:50.505 --> 01:02:51.767
I'm their mama.

1003
01:02:53.987 --> 01:02:57.033
I can't just leave 'em alone.

1004
01:02:57.207 --> 01:02:58.556
No. you can't.

1005
01:03:05.302 --> 01:03:09.524
I really believed it was
gon' work out with Phil.

1006
01:03:11.482 --> 01:03:12.570
I really did.

1007
01:03:18.141 --> 01:03:22.232
But it's over.

1008
01:03:25.235 --> 01:03:27.672
I just don't know what to do.

1009
01:03:34.418 --> 01:03:35.289
Well.

1010
01:03:39.946 --> 01:03:42.818
you can start by gettin'
up off the bathroom floor.

1011
01:03:49.259 --> 01:03:54.221
When I was little. and
Mama was in the hospital.

1012
01:03:56.353 --> 01:03:58.051
and Daddy was on the oil rigs.

1013
01:04:00.880 --> 01:04:03.099
I used to cry myself to sleep every night.

1014
01:04:06.189 --> 01:04:07.016
And then

1015
01:04:08.670 --> 01:04:10.628
one Sunday.

1016
01:04:10.802 --> 01:04:15.024
I heard the preacher down at church sayin'

1017
01:04:15.198 --> 01:04:17.026
that at some point in our lives.

1018
01:04:18.636 --> 01:04:23.424
we are all going to
feel desperately alone.

1019
01:04:25.905 --> 01:04:30.866
like we're the only soul
in the whole entire world.

1020
01:04:31.040 --> 01:04:34.696
and that that would be
the most important moment

1021
01:04:34.870 --> 01:04:36.524
in our whole entire lives

1022
01:04:38.134 --> 01:04:42.573
because when we realize that with Jesus.

1023
01:04:44.358 --> 01:04:46.099
we ain't never alone.

1024
01:04:49.276 --> 01:04:50.103
So.

1025
01:04:52.409 --> 01:04:55.064
I stopped cryin' myself to sleep at night.

1026
01:04:56.936 --> 01:04:59.416
and I started prayin' instead.

1027
01:05:02.202 --> 01:05:04.639
I'll watch the boys tomorrow.

1028
01:05:06.032 --> 01:05:07.772
There's someone you gotta go see.

1029
01:05:23.440 --> 01:05:25.312
Hey. that was a good one.

1030
01:05:25.486 --> 01:05:26.574
I appreciate ya.

1031
01:05:26.748 --> 01:05:29.794
God bless ya. I'll see ya on Wednesday.

1032
01:05:39.369 --> 01:05:40.675
Pastor Smith?

1033
01:05:40.849 --> 01:05:42.198
Yeah?

1034
01:05:42.372 --> 01:05:43.199
Hi.

1035
01:05:44.113 --> 01:05:45.027
I'm Kay Robertson.

1036
01:05:46.507 --> 01:05:47.899
Right.

1037
01:05:48.074 --> 01:05:49.814
Jan told me you might stop by.

1038
01:05:49.989 --> 01:05:51.425
It's good to see you again. Miss Kay.

1039
01:05:51.599 --> 01:05:52.643
It's been a bit.

1040
01:05:53.601 --> 01:05:56.908
I'm really sorry about my husband.

1041
01:05:58.910 --> 01:06:01.913
The first time at the bar-

1042
01:06:02.088 --> 01:06:03.045
Would it surprise you if I told you

1043
01:06:03.219 --> 01:06:04.742
I get that reaction a lot?

1044
01:06:07.484 --> 01:06:08.311
I guess not.

1045
01:06:09.486 --> 01:06:10.531
How's your husband?

1046
01:06:17.146 --> 01:06:19.148
He kicked us outta the house yesterday.

1047
01:06:20.802 --> 01:06:21.933
Me and my three boys.

1048
01:06:26.155 --> 01:06:27.548
Sorry to hear that.

1049
01:06:30.681 --> 01:06:32.640
Look. Jan said to come talk to you.

1050
01:06:34.642 --> 01:06:36.600
maybe you might be able to help us out.

1051
01:06:38.472 --> 01:06:42.432
But I don't really know
what I'm doin' here.

1052
01:06:43.868 --> 01:06:46.088
or what even to say and...

1053
01:06:52.877 --> 01:06:57.404
I guess I got into some
trouble last night.

1054
01:06:59.536 --> 01:07:00.581
thinkin' about some things

1055
01:07:00.755 --> 01:07:02.365
I shouldn't have been thinkin' about.

1056
01:07:04.976 --> 01:07:05.847
And...

1057
01:07:07.327 --> 01:07:08.719
I'm really sorry.

1058
01:07:08.893 --> 01:07:10.547
You must be so busy.

1059
01:07:10.721 --> 01:07:11.940
It's not a problem.

1060
01:07:13.985 --> 01:07:14.856
Truly.

1061
01:07:18.381 --> 01:07:19.556
You know. Miss Kay. it's the strangest

1062
01:07:19.730 --> 01:07:20.775
thing you should come by.

1063
01:07:20.949 --> 01:07:23.778
I was just now right now in a meetin'

1064
01:07:23.952 --> 01:07:25.519
and we was talkin' about what

1065
01:07:25.693 --> 01:07:26.911
to do with one of our little places

1066
01:07:27.086 --> 01:07:28.391
that just became vacant.

1067
01:07:29.784 --> 01:07:32.613
In fact. it's right over there.

1068
01:07:33.440 --> 01:07:34.919
It's right across the street.

1069
01:07:35.877 --> 01:07:37.008
Now. does that sound like somethin'

1070
01:07:37.183 --> 01:07:39.098
you and your boys might be interested in?

1071
01:07:44.973 --> 01:07:47.671
I don't know what to say. Pastor Smith.

1072
01:07:47.845 --> 01:07:49.760
Just Bill is fine.

1073
01:07:52.241 --> 01:07:54.765
Or Pastor Bill if you wanna be formal. hm?

1074
01:07:57.725 --> 01:07:58.421
Come on.

1075
01:08:06.951 --> 01:08:08.779
So we live here now?

1076
01:08:09.693 --> 01:08:10.564
Yeah.

1077
01:08:12.087 --> 01:08:13.393
This is a gift.

1078
01:08:14.524 --> 01:08:16.265
We're gonna take real
good care of it. you hear?

1079
01:08:26.623 --> 01:08:29.670
Kay got a job
and took care of the boys.

1080
01:08:29.844 --> 01:08:31.062
She was determined to make somethin'

1081
01:08:31.237 --> 01:08:32.586
of a life for them.

1082
01:08:35.110 --> 01:08:38.331
As for me. I finally had my freedom.

1083
01:08:39.636 --> 01:08:42.248
but it certainly didn't feel
like I thought it would.

1084
01:08:44.685 --> 01:08:45.555
Phil!

1085
01:08:48.906 --> 01:08:50.473
Phil. you in there?

1086
01:08:55.565 --> 01:08:57.176
As I live and breathe.

1087
01:08:58.089 --> 01:09:00.527
Man. I got a call from Nancy
down at the sheriff's station.

1088
01:09:00.701 --> 01:09:02.137
They found your truck completely totaled

1089
01:09:02.311 --> 01:09:03.747
but couldn't find your body.

1090
01:09:06.097 --> 01:09:07.664
I done a lotta crazy things in my life

1091
01:09:07.838 --> 01:09:09.231
but I ain't never done smashed

1092
01:09:09.405 --> 01:09:10.972
my truck up good enough to be canned

1093
01:09:11.146 --> 01:09:12.452
and put on the shelf in it.

1094
01:09:15.498 --> 01:09:16.891
Who's a man?

1095
01:09:20.416 --> 01:09:21.635
Hell. I'd offer to help you clean up.

1096
01:09:21.809 --> 01:09:24.420
but this is a lost cause.

1097
01:09:27.467 --> 01:09:28.772
This a gar hole. son.

1098
01:09:32.602 --> 01:09:33.473
What's the day?

1099
01:09:35.039 --> 01:09:36.693
Sunday.

1100
01:09:36.867 --> 01:09:39.696
♪ I heard an old. old story ♪

1101
01:09:39.870 --> 01:09:43.352
♪ How a savior came from glory ♪

1102
01:09:43.526 --> 01:09:47.226
♪ How he gave his life on Calvary ♪

1103
01:09:47.400 --> 01:09:51.012
♪ To save a wretch like me ♪

1104
01:09:51.186 --> 01:09:54.798
♪ I heard about his groaning ♪

1105
01:09:54.972 --> 01:09:58.715
♪ Of his precious blood atoning ♪

1106
01:09:58.889 --> 01:10:02.284
♪ Then I repented of my sins ♪

1107
01:10:02.458 --> 01:10:05.635
♪ And won the victory ♪

1108
01:10:08.334 --> 01:10:10.249
Mama. can we take those?

1109
01:10:11.032 --> 01:10:12.033
No. Alan.

1110
01:10:12.207 --> 01:10:13.077
Those are for kids that don't get

1111
01:10:13.252 --> 01:10:14.862
no presents at Christmas.

1112
01:10:17.821 --> 01:10:18.648
Okay.

1113
01:10:19.954 --> 01:10:20.955
But just a few.

1114
01:10:21.129 --> 01:10:22.478
Leave some for the other kids.

1115
01:10:55.468 --> 01:10:56.556
Get outta here!

1116
01:10:56.730 --> 01:10:57.557
Go!

1117
01:11:01.038 --> 01:11:04.128
She can't help it. it's
in her blood or somethin'.

1118
01:11:04.303 --> 01:11:06.522
We got that blood in us?

1119
01:11:06.696 --> 01:11:08.045
Don't know. but we'll always

1120
01:11:08.219 --> 01:11:11.048
look out for each other won't we?

1121
01:11:11.222 --> 01:11:13.355
You mean that. Phil?

1122
01:11:13.529 --> 01:11:15.139
Of course I do. Jan.

1123
01:11:28.588 --> 01:11:29.806
- Are we there yet?
- Are we there yet?

1124
01:11:29.980 --> 01:11:31.112
- Are we there yet?
- Not yet.

1125
01:11:31.286 --> 01:11:33.288
- Are we there yet?
- Not yet.

1126
01:11:33.462 --> 01:11:35.116
Uncle Si. how much further?

1127
01:11:35.290 --> 01:11:36.509
Oh. Lord.

1128
01:11:36.683 --> 01:11:37.771
What did I say?

1129
01:11:37.945 --> 01:11:39.425
If we come. no complainin'.

1130
01:11:39.599 --> 01:11:41.296
Uh huh. what are you doin'. Alan?

1131
01:11:41.470 --> 01:11:43.167
Jase. what's he doin'?

1132
01:11:43.342 --> 01:11:44.255
Complaining.

1133
01:11:44.430 --> 01:11:46.170
That's right. uh huh.

1134
01:11:49.783 --> 01:11:52.438
Phil. it's Si. are you in there?

1135
01:11:59.793 --> 01:12:01.360
You made it back.

1136
01:12:07.017 --> 01:12:07.888
I did.

1137
01:12:10.325 --> 01:12:11.195
I did.

1138
01:12:13.110 --> 01:12:14.329
It's good to see ya.

1139
01:12:15.852 --> 01:12:17.419
Look. I knew I'd find you out here.

1140
01:12:17.593 --> 01:12:18.942
but maybe I shoulda called.

1141
01:12:19.116 --> 01:12:21.641
givin' ya time to clean
up the place a bit.

1142
01:12:24.034 --> 01:12:26.863
Ya ain't gotta live like
no wild man anymore. Phil.

1143
01:12:33.174 --> 01:12:35.002
It's better for me out here.

1144
01:12:35.176 --> 01:12:37.091
Oh. Phil. how's that?

1145
01:12:38.397 --> 01:12:39.876
I don't have to be anything but me.

1146
01:12:40.050 --> 01:12:42.444
Well. that may be true.

1147
01:12:42.618 --> 01:12:44.838
but hey. I think you should come back.

1148
01:12:45.012 --> 01:12:45.839
You know?

1149
01:12:47.275 --> 01:12:48.842
Work on some things.

1150
01:12:52.411 --> 01:12:53.803
And what work would I need?

1151
01:12:53.977 --> 01:12:57.459
Well. I been hearin'
about a lotta things.

1152
01:13:01.811 --> 01:13:02.812
Ain't much from fit to talk about

1153
01:13:02.986 --> 01:13:05.728
in front of little ears. though.

1154
01:13:05.902 --> 01:13:07.164
Daddy?

1155
01:13:08.992 --> 01:13:10.211
Al?

1156
01:13:10.385 --> 01:13:11.255
Jase?

1157
01:13:13.083 --> 01:13:15.259
What you doin' here. boys?

1158
01:13:17.087 --> 01:13:17.914
Come on. now.

1159
01:13:19.525 --> 01:13:21.744
Ain't ya gonna give your pa a hug?

1160
01:13:21.918 --> 01:13:22.876
What?

1161
01:13:23.050 --> 01:13:24.704
What. you don't recognize me?

1162
01:13:24.878 --> 01:13:27.707
Hey. Jase. hey. hey. hey.
hey. it's okay. it's okay.

1163
01:13:27.881 --> 01:13:29.056
You all right?

1164
01:13:30.884 --> 01:13:33.277
I think y'all should leave.

1165
01:13:33.452 --> 01:13:34.453
Yeah.

1166
01:13:34.627 --> 01:13:37.151
Say hi to your mama for me. boys.

1167
01:13:37.325 --> 01:13:39.806
- You change your mind-
- I'll see ya around. Si.

1168
01:13:41.024 --> 01:13:41.982
Come on. boys.

1169
01:13:53.123 --> 01:13:55.735
All right. boys. hungry?

1170
01:13:55.909 --> 01:13:57.606
- Eat. eat!
- Yeah.

1171
01:13:59.478 --> 01:14:01.305
Alan. you wanna lead us?

1172
01:14:02.176 --> 01:14:03.307
Good boy.

1173
01:14:05.962 --> 01:14:08.704
Dear Jesus. I miss my daddy.

1174
01:14:08.878 --> 01:14:10.271
Please make him a good man.

1175
01:14:11.751 --> 01:14:12.839
Amen.

1176
01:14:15.189 --> 01:14:16.059
All right.

1177
01:14:17.104 --> 01:14:18.497
What do you want?

1178
01:14:19.367 --> 01:14:20.629
Some of this?

1179
01:14:20.803 --> 01:14:21.978
They're yum.

1180
01:14:22.152 --> 01:14:25.199
All right.

1181
01:14:25.373 --> 01:14:26.722
Thank you.

1182
01:15:13.421 --> 01:15:16.511
You're the only girl for me.

1183
01:15:17.947 --> 01:15:20.254
You gon' make a good dad.

1184
01:15:21.298 --> 01:15:22.561
I'm proud of you.

1185
01:15:24.040 --> 01:15:24.954
I love you.

1186
01:16:25.188 --> 01:16:27.234
I can't.

1187
01:16:27.408 --> 01:16:28.278
I can't!

1188
01:16:29.932 --> 01:16:31.194
I can't!

1189
01:17:48.402 --> 01:17:50.186
You drunk right now?

1190
01:17:57.411 --> 01:17:58.804
Nope.

1191
01:18:11.077 --> 01:18:13.775
I think I saw him. Miss Kay.

1192
01:18:18.171 --> 01:18:19.476
Who?

1193
01:18:22.001 --> 01:18:23.437
The devil.

1194
01:18:32.185 --> 01:18:34.622
I think he might be me.

1195
01:18:43.631 --> 01:18:45.502
I'll quit drinkin' this time.

1196
01:18:45.676 --> 01:18:47.330
I promise.

1197
01:18:47.504 --> 01:18:48.375
No.

1198
01:18:51.030 --> 01:18:53.032
I'm done with promisin'.

1199
01:18:59.560 --> 01:19:00.430
Kay!

1200
01:19:02.302 --> 01:19:03.129
I'm sorry.

1201
01:19:04.086 --> 01:19:05.261
I messed it all up.

1202
01:19:05.435 --> 01:19:06.523
Miss Kay!

1203
01:19:10.832 --> 01:19:11.702
Phil.

1204
01:19:16.055 --> 01:19:17.230
you need help.

1205
01:19:20.755 --> 01:19:22.844
More help than me and
the boys can give ya.

1206
01:19:27.718 --> 01:19:29.329
You need to change.

1207
01:19:36.815 --> 01:19:37.772
Miss Kay.

1208
01:19:40.557 --> 01:19:42.429
I'll do anything for you and the boys.

1209
01:19:46.868 --> 01:19:47.738
Anything.

1210
01:19:50.872 --> 01:19:51.742
I swear.

1211
01:20:09.673 --> 01:20:11.153
Gimme a minute.

1212
01:20:11.327 --> 01:20:13.199
It's really okay. Phil.

1213
01:20:18.204 --> 01:20:19.031
Uh...

1214
01:20:22.251 --> 01:20:23.252
You know.

1215
01:20:25.211 --> 01:20:27.039
it's beautiful out back.

1216
01:20:27.213 --> 01:20:28.127
You wanna?

1217
01:20:28.301 --> 01:20:29.041
How 'bout you meet me out there?

1218
01:21:06.992 --> 01:21:07.644
Nah.

1219
01:21:09.733 --> 01:21:11.997
Not quite sure what to say.

1220
01:21:13.346 --> 01:21:15.696
Just say whatever's
on your mind. Phil.

1221
01:21:29.797 --> 01:21:31.233
I guess it were...

1222
01:21:35.803 --> 01:21:38.588
Everything I ever touch is goin' to hell.

1223
01:21:41.548 --> 01:21:44.943
You know what I would do if everything

1224
01:21:45.117 --> 01:21:46.814
I touched went to hell?

1225
01:21:50.470 --> 01:21:51.297
What's that?

1226
01:22:06.399 --> 01:22:08.618
I'd quit touchin' things.

1227
01:22:16.931 --> 01:22:20.108
Do you know what most
stories have in common?

1228
01:22:23.851 --> 01:22:27.028
Most of 'em are about

1229
01:22:29.552 --> 01:22:31.598
climbin' the mountain.

1230
01:22:32.468 --> 01:22:34.775
becomin' a God.

1231
01:22:37.125 --> 01:22:39.345
provin' just how good you are.

1232
01:22:40.433 --> 01:22:42.348
that you're good enough.

1233
01:22:49.529 --> 01:22:51.009
It's a whole different story.

1234
01:22:56.840 --> 01:23:00.627
This is about God comin'
down from the mountain.

1235
01:23:02.759 --> 01:23:07.329
comin' to you. tellin' you.

1236
01:23:08.765 --> 01:23:12.247
"Phil. you ain't got nothin' to prove."

1237
01:23:18.819 --> 01:23:20.690
Hey. that chip on your shoulder.

1238
01:23:22.823 --> 01:23:25.130
shame you've had your whole life.

1239
01:23:28.307 --> 01:23:30.483
It don't mean nothin' to Him.

1240
01:23:31.745 --> 01:23:33.181
In fact.

1241
01:23:37.403 --> 01:23:39.970
He come down to take that away.

1242
01:23:49.067 --> 01:23:51.895
That sounds too good to be true.

1243
01:23:53.506 --> 01:23:54.333
Oh.

1244
01:23:57.162 --> 01:23:59.512
it's too good for all of us.

1245
01:24:03.429 --> 01:24:04.952
How's it happen?

1246
01:24:06.432 --> 01:24:08.347
You got to die. Phil.

1247
01:24:14.179 --> 01:24:16.877
And then you need to be born again.

1248
01:24:30.630 --> 01:24:31.848
I'm ready.

1249
01:24:44.296 --> 01:24:46.211
Your daddy's lived a hard life.

1250
01:24:49.475 --> 01:24:50.432
That ends today.

1251
01:24:53.261 --> 01:24:54.871
We gon' bury that old man.

1252
01:24:59.354 --> 01:25:01.443
This dirty river water represents a grave.

1253
01:25:02.662 --> 01:25:07.580
But. a new man is gonna rise up.

1254
01:25:09.190 --> 01:25:11.975
Phil. from this day forth.

1255
01:25:12.150 --> 01:25:14.587
who's gonna be the lord in your life?

1256
01:25:14.761 --> 01:25:16.066
Jesus Christ.

1257
01:25:17.677 --> 01:25:19.461
With that confession.

1258
01:25:19.635 --> 01:25:21.507
I baptize you in the
name of the Father. Son.

1259
01:25:21.681 --> 01:25:25.032
and Holy Ghost for the
forgiveness of your sins.

1260
01:25:38.872 --> 01:25:39.742
You ready?

1261
01:26:16.214 --> 01:26:17.476
All right brother!

1262
01:26:20.696 --> 01:26:21.306
Woo!

1263
01:26:27.921 --> 01:26:29.444
♪ Dashin' through the snow ♪

1264
01:26:29.618 --> 01:26:31.707
♪ In a one-horse open sleigh ♪

1265
01:26:31.881 --> 01:26:33.927
♪ O'er the fields we go ♪

1266
01:26:34.101 --> 01:26:35.015
Good boy.

1267
01:26:35.189 --> 01:26:36.495
♪ Laughin' all the way ♪

1268
01:26:38.366 --> 01:26:39.802
I know.

1269
01:26:39.976 --> 01:26:41.587
- Daddy?
- Hm?

1270
01:26:41.761 --> 01:26:43.328
When do you have to leave?

1271
01:26:43.502 --> 01:26:44.416
What you mean?

1272
01:26:44.590 --> 01:26:45.765
Don't you got somewhere to be?

1273
01:26:45.939 --> 01:26:48.768
I ain't got nowhere to be.

1274
01:26:48.942 --> 01:26:50.770
You good with that?

1275
01:26:50.944 --> 01:26:51.901
All right.

1276
01:26:52.075 --> 01:26:53.947
♪ Jingle all the way ♪

1277
01:26:54.121 --> 01:26:58.908
♪ Oh. what fun it is to ride
in a one-horse open sleigh ♪

1278
01:26:59.605 --> 01:27:03.348
♪ Jingle bells. jingle bells ♪

1279
01:27:05.175 --> 01:27:06.916
Mm. smells good.

1280
01:27:25.892 --> 01:27:28.068
Hey. Jase. lemme see that.

1281
01:27:35.858 --> 01:27:37.033
Thanks. buddy.

1282
01:28:03.059 --> 01:28:06.324
You gonna buy Jase a
new one now you broke it?

1283
01:28:06.498 --> 01:28:08.978
I didn't break it. just fixin' it.

1284
01:28:15.724 --> 01:28:18.336
You know. I had a moment today.

1285
01:28:20.163 --> 01:28:23.297
Maybe bein' sober for the
first time in a long time.

1286
01:28:26.431 --> 01:28:28.258
Lots of people make duck calls. right?

1287
01:28:28.433 --> 01:28:30.348
They sound like ducks. sure.

1288
01:28:30.522 --> 01:28:32.567
but pintails sure don't
sound like a mallard.

1289
01:28:32.741 --> 01:28:37.137
just as much as I don't
sound like you when I talk.

1290
01:28:37.311 --> 01:28:37.964
So what?

1291
01:28:38.138 --> 01:28:39.182
"So what?"

1292
01:28:49.062 --> 01:28:50.542
Thanks for bein' here today.

1293
01:28:53.022 --> 01:28:54.197
Meant a lot to the boys.

1294
01:29:01.379 --> 01:29:02.380
I've been tryin'.

1295
01:29:06.949 --> 01:29:08.342
You been tryin'.

1296
01:29:11.954 --> 01:29:14.522
I know it ain't been perfect.

1297
01:29:16.698 --> 01:29:17.525
No.

1298
01:29:20.006 --> 01:29:24.053
Truth is. I been fightin'
for us for 10 years.

1299
01:29:27.187 --> 01:29:28.667
I just had nothin' left in me.

1300
01:29:32.453 --> 01:29:35.021
Then I saw you get baptized in that river

1301
01:29:35.195 --> 01:29:36.762
and I was

1302
01:29:38.024 --> 01:29:39.417
I was full.

1303
01:29:40.505 --> 01:29:42.028
I was so full of joy.

1304
01:29:47.947 --> 01:29:49.339
My heart was so full.

1305
01:29:52.908 --> 01:29:55.258
and I had this little voice.

1306
01:29:58.566 --> 01:30:01.351
This naggin' voice sayin'

1307
01:30:01.526 --> 01:30:04.050
it's just gonna start all over again.

1308
01:30:05.921 --> 01:30:07.662
And you was gonna break our hearts.

1309
01:30:10.273 --> 01:30:11.797
I'm sorry. Miss Kay.

1310
01:30:13.973 --> 01:30:14.800
Truly.

1311
01:30:17.672 --> 01:30:20.545
I never wanna put you through that again.

1312
01:30:26.507 --> 01:30:28.857
You remember why you quit football?

1313
01:30:32.731 --> 01:30:34.384
It was huntin' season.

1314
01:30:36.169 --> 01:30:37.736
Well. partly 'cause you are stubborn

1315
01:30:37.910 --> 01:30:39.389
as an ox stuck in mud.

1316
01:30:43.568 --> 01:30:46.832
But the other part. that
was 'cause you wanted

1317
01:30:47.006 --> 01:30:48.834
to take care of us.

1318
01:30:50.662 --> 01:30:54.535
Take care of your family
just like you always had.

1319
01:30:56.624 --> 01:30:59.061
Now look. I know you're gonna stumble.

1320
01:30:59.235 --> 01:31:01.890
I know it ain't gon' be perfect.

1321
01:31:04.719 --> 01:31:07.069
But maybe if you just keep that in mind.

1322
01:31:09.942 --> 01:31:13.293
how much you really do love your family.

1323
01:31:14.337 --> 01:31:15.208
Yeah.

1324
01:31:16.122 --> 01:31:20.126
Maybe it might be right
to get away from it all.

1325
01:31:21.127 --> 01:31:23.129
Old friends. temptation.

1326
01:31:26.567 --> 01:31:28.526
We'll get ourselves a little place.

1327
01:31:28.700 --> 01:31:30.615
I could fish the river.

1328
01:31:32.530 --> 01:31:36.316
Well now. that might be an idea. Phil.

1329
01:31:41.103 --> 01:31:42.452
Merry Christmas.

1330
01:31:44.237 --> 01:31:45.934
Merry Christmas. Miss Kay.

1331
01:32:17.618 --> 01:32:21.535
Before I came along. everyone
thought the duck calls people

1332
01:32:21.709 --> 01:32:23.363
were makin' were great.

1333
01:32:23.537 --> 01:32:27.889
but truth is. they were missin' somethin'.

1334
01:32:28.063 --> 01:32:29.412
They looked the same.

1335
01:32:29.587 --> 01:32:30.718
You know. one duck call
looked like another.

1336
01:32:30.892 --> 01:32:35.897
but on the inside. somethin' had changed.

1337
01:32:41.816 --> 01:32:43.035
Turns out.

1338
01:32:46.081 --> 01:32:48.214
that could make all the difference.

1339
01:33:05.144 --> 01:33:05.971
Phil?

1340
01:33:06.928 --> 01:33:07.581
Phil?

1341
01:33:10.105 --> 01:33:11.759
There he is.

1342
01:33:14.457 --> 01:33:16.372
My man.

1343
01:33:16.546 --> 01:33:17.765
Keep it down.

1344
01:33:17.939 --> 01:33:19.593
Everyone's still sleepin' in there.

1345
01:33:19.767 --> 01:33:21.813
Well. they're missin'
out on the best fish. then.

1346
01:33:21.987 --> 01:33:23.641
We come to get ya. get your things.

1347
01:33:23.815 --> 01:33:25.468
It's a day after Christmas tradition.

1348
01:33:25.643 --> 01:33:26.948
We'll hit the water.

1349
01:33:27.122 --> 01:33:29.255
and head to State Line
Road for a party after.

1350
01:33:31.561 --> 01:33:33.215
I ain't drinkin' anymore. boys.

1351
01:33:36.175 --> 01:33:38.612
The Phil you come lookin'
for is dead and buried.

1352
01:33:43.530 --> 01:33:46.098
Dang. you startin' to scare me. Phil.

1353
01:33:46.272 --> 01:33:49.710
Look. it's been ages
since you partied with us.

1354
01:33:49.884 --> 01:33:50.885
Come on. now.

1355
01:33:51.059 --> 01:33:52.974
You know it's gon' be a grand time.

1356
01:33:53.148 --> 01:33:54.846
Get your freedom back for a night.

1357
01:33:56.238 --> 01:33:57.152
Well?

1358
01:33:58.023 --> 01:33:58.893
What's it gonna be?

1359
01:34:00.155 --> 01:34:01.156
Who's a man?

1360
01:34:49.683 --> 01:34:50.553
Daddy?

1361
01:34:50.728 --> 01:34:53.600
Shh. wake your brother.

1362
01:34:53.774 --> 01:34:55.254
Put your warm clothes on.

1363
01:34:55.428 --> 01:34:58.039
Your mama said it was okay.

1364
01:34:58.213 --> 01:34:58.866
Come on.

1365
01:35:11.923 --> 01:35:13.098
Come on. boys.

1366
01:35:17.189 --> 01:35:18.843
Stay close to Daddy.

1367
01:35:20.758 --> 01:35:21.454
Good boy.

1368
01:35:26.241 --> 01:35:30.942
Shh.

1369
01:35:32.552 --> 01:35:33.814
Look right there.

1370
01:35:40.603 --> 01:35:42.040
You try.

1371
01:35:46.218 --> 01:35:47.088
You try boy.

1372
01:35:57.969 --> 01:36:01.711
I started taking the kids
to the woods a lot more.

1373
01:36:01.886 --> 01:36:04.584
teachin' 'em about huntin'.

1374
01:36:04.758 --> 01:36:08.762
I'm just down here. fishin'. huntin'.

1375
01:36:10.111 --> 01:36:11.721
tryin' to sell these duck calls.

1376
01:36:14.768 --> 01:36:17.118
In the end I guess Kay
got her pioneer lifestyle

1377
01:36:17.292 --> 01:36:21.296
and I got my family back.

1378
01:36:24.343 --> 01:36:25.648
not because I deserved it.

1379
01:36:28.651 --> 01:36:29.827
Lord knows I didn't.

1380
01:36:33.700 --> 01:36:35.963
But that's the thing I learned about God.

1381
01:36:39.662 --> 01:36:41.186
We don't have to be good enough

1382
01:36:44.145 --> 01:36:45.712
'cause he's good enough for us.

1383
01:36:47.627 --> 01:36:49.107
I finally figured it out.

1384
01:36:51.370 --> 01:36:52.588
Just took a little time.

1385
01:37:02.468 --> 01:37:03.425
Yeah. well.

1386
01:37:06.646 --> 01:37:09.344
seems like I might not have
as much time as I thought.

1387
01:37:13.348 --> 01:37:14.697
How so?

1388
01:37:19.920 --> 01:37:22.053
Well. I ain't told
anybody else this but.

1389
01:37:25.665 --> 01:37:26.666
it's my heart.

1390
01:37:34.761 --> 01:37:36.241
I got a aneurysm.

1391
01:37:41.159 --> 01:37:45.293
Doctor said it could be two years.

1392
01:37:47.208 --> 01:37:47.905
two months.

1393
01:37:48.079 --> 01:37:48.906
Heck.

1394
01:37:51.256 --> 01:37:52.083
two days.

1395
01:37:55.042 --> 01:37:56.348
Any moment. really.

1396
01:38:04.747 --> 01:38:08.926
You called me up and
asked me to tell you

1397
01:38:10.797 --> 01:38:14.932
what I'd heard. how I got out.

1398
01:38:15.106 --> 01:38:16.411
made a life for myself.

1399
01:38:20.459 --> 01:38:24.289
Well. that's the secret. I didn't do it.

1400
01:38:27.727 --> 01:38:30.817
Only God can pull off a move like that

1401
01:38:33.167 --> 01:38:34.864
because of Jesus.

1402
01:38:36.779 --> 01:38:38.738
Stop always makin' it only about me.

1403
01:38:40.218 --> 01:38:41.175
That's what I finally learned.

1404
01:38:41.349 --> 01:38:43.525
how to give my life away.

1405
01:38:46.441 --> 01:38:47.877
Funny thing is. once I gave it up.

1406
01:38:48.052 --> 01:38:49.531
that's when I got it all back.

1407
01:38:51.142 --> 01:38:53.318
Everything I been chasin' all these years.

1408
01:38:55.668 --> 01:38:56.756
Funny how that works.

1409
01:38:59.977 --> 01:39:02.805
How you gotta come to the end of yourself

1410
01:39:04.633 --> 01:39:06.331
to find the beginning of God.

1411
01:39:12.641 --> 01:39:13.903
I gotta tell you. Phil.

1412
01:39:19.170 --> 01:39:20.823
that's startin' to make a lotta sense.

1413
01:39:42.845 --> 01:39:47.459
♪ As I travel ♪

1414
01:39:47.633 --> 01:39:51.245
♪ On life's pathway ♪

1415
01:39:51.419 --> 01:39:53.552
♪ Knowing not what years may hold ♪

1416
01:40:00.080 --> 01:40:03.127
♪ As I ponder ♪

1417
01:40:03.301 --> 01:40:06.391
♪ Hope grows fonder ♪

1418
01:40:06.565 --> 01:40:07.957
Come on. boys.

1419
01:40:08.132 --> 01:40:08.958
♪ Precious memories flood my soul ♪

1420
01:40:09.133 --> 01:40:11.874
Hey.

1421
01:40:17.184 --> 01:40:19.186
- Oh. gravy?
- Gravy.

1422
01:40:21.449 --> 01:40:24.061
♪ How they linger ♪

1423
01:40:24.235 --> 01:40:28.065
♪ How they ever flood my soul ♪

1424
01:40:32.765 --> 01:40:34.201
We're happy to have you.

1425
01:40:34.375 --> 01:40:35.376
Thank you.

1426
01:40:38.553 --> 01:40:39.380
Hello.

1427
01:40:40.468 --> 01:40:41.643
Thank y'all for comin'.

1428
01:40:44.429 --> 01:40:46.344
Why don't we say a little prayer?

1429
01:40:50.826 --> 01:40:51.697
Father.

1430
01:40:52.698 --> 01:40:55.222
we thank you for another
great day on planet Earth.

1431
01:40:57.268 --> 01:40:59.531
for the bunch of ducks
we killed this mornin'.

1432
01:41:00.488 --> 01:41:01.924
and the grub on this table.

1433
01:41:04.188 --> 01:41:06.973
In Jesus' name we pray. amen.

1434
01:41:08.844 --> 01:41:09.889
Amen.

1435
01:41:10.803 --> 01:41:11.804
Y'all dig in.

1436
01:41:15.024 --> 01:41:19.159
♪ Unseen angels ♪

1437
01:41:19.333 --> 01:41:23.250
♪ Sent from heaven somewhere to my soul ♪

1438
01:41:26.601 --> 01:41:27.472
Who got that apple butter?

1439
01:41:27.646 --> 01:41:30.388
♪ How they linger ♪

1440
01:41:31.954 --> 01:41:34.914
Stop hoggin' the corn down
there. will you pass it down?

1441
